Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.60,0:02:42.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ready?\N准备好了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.15,0:03:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go.\N开始吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.32,0:03:58.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the stage,\N欢迎登上舞台，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.63,0:04:10.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,NVIDIA founder and CEO, Jensen Huang.\N英伟达创始人兼首席执行官黄仁勋。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.60,0:04:13.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello, Las Vegas.\N大家好，拉斯维加斯。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.96,0:04:16.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Happy New Year.\N新年快乐。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.24,0:04:18.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to CES.\N欢迎参加CES。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.00,0:04:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we have about 15 keynotes worth of material to pack in here.\N嗯，我们这儿得塞进大约15场主题演讲的内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.08,0:04:25.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm so happy to see all of you.\N我非常高兴见到大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.30,0:04:27.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,You got 3,000 people in this auditorium.\N这个礼堂里有3000人。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.18,0:04:29.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's 2,000 people in the courtyard watching us.\N广场上有2000人在观看我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.96,0:04:35.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's another thousand people apparently in the fourth floor where there were supposed to be NVIDIA show floors,\N据说还有1000人在四楼，那里本该是英伟达的展区，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.38,0:04:42.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,all watching this keynote, and of course, millions around the world are going to be watching this to kick off this new year.\N所有正在观看这场主题演讲的人，当然，全球数百万观众也将通过这场演讲迎接新的一年。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.96,0:04:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, every 10 to 15 years, the computer industry resets.\N每隔10到15年，计算机产业就会迎来一次重置。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.00,0:04:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,A new platform shift happens.\N一次新的平台转型正在发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.64,0:04:57.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,From mainframe to PC, PC to internet, internet to cloud, cloud to mobile.\N从大型机到个人电脑，从个人电脑到互联网，从互联网到云，从云到移动设备。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.96,0:05:03.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each time, the world of applications target a new platform.\N每一次，应用领域都会转向新的平台。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.73,0:05:05.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why it's called a platform shift.\N这就是为什么它被称为平台转型。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.70,0:05:09.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,You write new applications for a new computer.\N你为新的计算机编写新的应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.96,0:05:18.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Except this time, there are two simultaneous platform shifts in fact happening at the same time.\N但这一次，实际上正同时发生两次平台转型。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.80,0:05:25.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,While we now move to AI, applications are now going to be built on top of AI.\N当我们转向AI时，应用将建立在AI之上。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.36,0:05:34.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,At first, people thought AIs are applications, and in fact, AIs are applications, but you're going to build applications on top of AIs.\N最初人们认为AI就是应用，而实际上AI确实是应用，但你将基于AI构建新的应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.12,0:05:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, in addition to that, how you run the software, how you develop the software fundamentally changed.\N此外，软件的运行方式和开发方式也从根本上发生了改变。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.16,0:05:49.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,The entire five-layer stack of the computer industry is being reinvented.\N计算机产业的整个五层架构正在被重新发明。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.64,0:05:54.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You no longer program the software, you train the software.\N你不再编写软件，而是训练软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.48,0:05:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't run it on CPUs, you run it on GPUs.\N你不再在 CPU 上运行它，而是在 GPU 上运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.92,0:06:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And whereas applications were pre-recorded, pre-compiled, and run on your device,\N以往的应用程序是预先录制、预先编译并在你的设备上运行的，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.72,0:06:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,now applications understand the context and generate every single pixel, every single token, completely from scratch every single time.\N现在的应用程序能够理解上下文，并每次从零开始生成每一个像素、每一个词元。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.12,0:06:23.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Computing has been fundamentally reshaped as result of accelerated computing, as result of artificial intelligence.\N由于加速计算和人工智能的推动，计算方式已从根本上被重塑。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.78,0:06:29.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single layer of that five-layer cake is now being reinvented.\N那个五层蛋糕的每一层如今都在被重新发明。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.52,0:06:39.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, what that means is some 10 trillion dollars or so of the last decade of computing is now being modernized to this new way of doing computing.\N换句话说，过去十年约一万亿美金的计算投入，如今正被现代化为这种新的计算方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.44,0:06:46.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,What that means is hundreds of billions of dollars, a couple hundred billion dollars in VC funding each year,\N这意味着每年数百亿甚至数百亿美元的风险投资资金，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.15,0:06:49.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,is going into modernizing and inventing this new world.\N正投入于这一新世界的现代化与创新。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.56,0:07:00.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what it means is a hundred trillion dollars of industry, several percent of which is R&D budget, is shifting over to artificial intelligence.\N这意味着数百万亿美元的产业，其中数个百分点的研发预算，正转向人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.08,0:07:02.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,People ask, "Where is the money coming from?"\N人们问：“钱从哪里来？”
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.28,0:07:04.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's where the money is coming from.\N钱就来自这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.84,0:07:13.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,The modernization of AI to AI, the shifting of R&D budgets from classical methods to now artificial intelligence methods.\N人工智能的现代化，研发预算从传统方法转向人工智能方法的转变。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.74,0:07:19.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Enormous amounts of investments coming into this industry, which explains why we're so busy.\N大量投资涌入这一行业，这解释了我们为何如此忙碌。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.34,0:07:21.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this last year was no difference.\N去年的情况也毫无例外。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.84,0:07:24.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This last year was incredible.\N去年简直令人难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.40,0:07:28.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This last year, there's a slide coming.\N去年，有一项关键进展正在浮现。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.40,0:07:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is what happens when you don't practice.\N这就是不练习的后果。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.92,0:07:34.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,2025 was an incredible year.\N2025 年是极其非凡的一年。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.92,0:07:39.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just see It seems like everything was happening all at the same time, and in fact, it probably was.\N似乎所有事情都在同一时间发生，事实上很可能确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.04,0:07:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first thing, of course, is scaling laws.\N首先，当然是缩放定律。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.96,0:07:51.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,In 20 15, the first language model that I thought was really going to make a difference made a huge difference.\N2015 年，我第一次认为真正能带来改变的语言模型带来了巨大影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.87,0:07:53.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was called BERT.\N它叫做 BERT。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.14,0:07:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,2017, transformers came.\N2017 年，Transformer 模型问世。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.24,0:08:06.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It wasn't until 5 years later, 2022, that ChatGPT moment happened, and it awakened the world to the possibilities of artificial intelligence.\N直到五年后的2022年，ChatGPT时刻才真正到来，它让全世界意识到人工智能的可能性。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.08,0:08:10.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Something very important happened a year after that.\N那之后一年，发生了一件非常重要的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.56,0:08:16.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first 01 model from ChatGPT, the first reasoning model, completely revolutionary,\NChatGPT推出的首个01模型，首个具备推理能力的模型，完全革命性的突破，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.36,0:08:21.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,invented this idea called test time scaling, which is very common sense common sensical thing.\N首次提出了“测试时扩展”这一概念，这其实是一个非常合乎常理的想法。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.89,0:08:29.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only do we pre-train a model to learn, we post-train it with our reinforcement learning so that it could learn skills.\N我们不仅对模型进行预训练以学习知识，还通过强化学习进行后训练，使其掌握技能。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.48,0:08:33.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now we also have test time scaling, which is another way of saying thinking.\N现在我们还拥有了测试时扩展，这本质上就是“思考”的另一种说法。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.80,0:08:35.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You think in real time.\N你在实时地进行思考。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.48,0:08:41.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these phases of artificial intelligence requires enormous amount of compute.\N人工智能发展的每一个阶段都需要巨大的算力支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.16,0:08:43.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the computing law continued to scale.\N而计算能力的提升仍在持续扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.06,0:08:46.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Large language models continued to get better.\N大型语言模型持续变得更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.24,0:08:48.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, another breakthrough happened.\N与此同时，另一项突破也发生了。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.43,0:08:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this breakthrough happened in 2024.\N这项突破发生在2024年。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.32,0:09:00.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Agentic systems starting to emerge, and 2025, it started to pervade to to proliferate just about everywhere.\N代理式系统开始涌现，到了2025年，它们开始无处不在地扩散。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.36,0:09:08.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Agentic models that have the ability to reason, look up information, do research, use tools,\N代理式模型具备推理、查找信息、开展研究、使用工具的能力，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.80,0:09:15.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,plan futures, simulate outcomes, all of a sudden started to solve very, very important problems.\N规划未来、模拟结果，突然间开始解决非常非常重要的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.19,0:09:22.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of my favorite agentic models is called Cursor, which revolutionized the way we do software programming at NVIDIA.\N我最喜欢的代理式模型之一叫Cursor，它彻底改变了英伟达进行软件编程的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.72,0:09:26.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Agentic systems are going to really take off from here.\N代理式系统将真正开始腾飞。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.64,0:09:28.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, there were other types of AI.\N当然，还有其他类型的AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.56,0:09:31.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We know that large language models isn't the only type of information.\N我们知道，大型语言模型并不是唯一的信息形式。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.73,0:09:39.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wherever the universe has information, wherever the universe has structure, we could teach a large language model,\N无论宇宙中何处存在信息，无论何处存在结构，我们都可以训练一个大型语言模型，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.50,0:09:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,a form of language model, to go understand that information, to understand its representation, and to turn that into an AI.\N一种语言模型形式，去理解这些信息，理解其表达方式，并将其转化为AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.08,0:09:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of the biggest, most important one is physical AI, AIs that understand the laws of nature.\N其中最大、最重要的一种是物理AI，即理解自然法则的AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.68,0:10:00.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, of course, physical AIs is about AIs interacting with the world.\N而物理AI则关乎AI与世界的互动。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.56,0:10:06.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the world itself has information encoded information, and that's called AI physics.\N但世界本身也编码了信息，这种信息被称为AI物理。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.11,0:10:11.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI that in the case of physical AI, you have AI that interacts with the physical world,\N人工智能在物理人工智能的情况下，是指与物理世界交互的人工智能，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.32,0:10:16.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you have AI physics, AI that understands the laws of physics.\N以及人工智能物理学，即理解物理定律的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.08,0:10:23.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, lastly, one of the most important things that happened last year, the advancement of open models.\N最后，去年最重要的事情之一，是开源模型的发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.16,0:10:30.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can now know that AI is going to proliferate everywhere when open source, when open innovation,\N现在我们可以确定，当开源、开放创新成为可能时，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.09,0:10:35.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,when innovation across every single company and every industry around the world is activated at the same time.\N当全球每一个公司和每一个行业同时被激活创新时，人工智能将无处不在。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.98,0:10:39.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Open models really took off last year.\N去年，开源模型真正开始腾飞。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.55,0:10:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, last year, we saw the advance of DeepSeek R1, the first open model that's a reasoning system.\N事实上，去年我们见证了 DeepSeek R1 的进步，这是首个具备推理能力的开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.72,0:10:57.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,It caught the world by surprise, and it activated literally this entire movement.\N它令世界感到震惊，并真正激活了整个运动。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.97,0:10:59.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really, really exciting work.\N真的非常令人激动的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.85,0:11:01.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're so happy with it.\N我们对此感到无比欣喜。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.40,0:11:10.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we have openings open model systems all over the world of all different kinds, and we now know that open models have also reached the frontier.\N如今，全球各地出现了各种各样的开源模型系统，我们如今也清楚，开源模型已经达到了前沿水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.77,0:11:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Still solidly is 6 months behind the frontier models,\N仍然比前沿模型落后约六个月。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.84,0:11:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,but every single 6 months a new model is emerging, and these models are getting smarter and smarter.\N但每隔六个月就会出现一个新模型，这些模型变得越来越聪明。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.12,0:11:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because of that, you could see the number of downloads has exploded.\N正因为如此，你可以看到下载量已经爆炸式增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.84,0:11:34.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,The number of downloads is growing so fast because startups want to participate in the AI revolution,\N下载量增长如此迅速，是因为初创公司想要参与人工智能革命，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.31,0:11:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,large companies want to, researchers want to, students want to, just about every single country wants to.\N大公司想要，研究人员想要，学生想要，几乎每个国家都想要。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.60,0:11:46.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,How is it possible that intelligence, the digital form of intelligence, will leave anyone behind?\N人工智能，这种数字化形式的智能，怎么可能让任何人落后呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.75,0:11:52.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, open models has really revolutionized artificial intelligence last year.\N因此，开放模型去年真正革新了人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.59,0:11:56.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,This entire industry is going to be reshaped as a result of that.\N由于这一变化，整个行业都将被重塑。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.16,0:11:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we had this inkling some time ago.\N现在，我们早些时候就已有所察觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.24,0:12:05.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,You might have heard that several years ago, we just started to build and operate our own AI supercomputers.\N你可能听说过，几年前我们就开始自行构建和运营自己的AI超级计算机。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.80,0:12:07.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,We call them DGX Clouds.\N我们称它们为DGX云。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.79,0:12:11.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,A lot of people asked, "Are you going to going into the cloud business?"\N很多人问：“你们会进入云业务吗？”
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.01,0:12:16.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,The answer is no. We're building these DGX supercomputers for our own use.\N答案是否定的。我们建造这些DGX超级计算机是供自己使用的。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.47,0:12:24.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, it turns out we have billions of dollars of supercomputers in operation, so that we could develop our open models.\N事实上，我们已有数十亿美元的超级计算机在运行，这使我们能够开发开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.70,0:12:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I am so pleased with the work that we're doing.\N我对我们正在做的工作感到非常高兴。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.16,0:12:31.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is starting to attract attention all over the world and all over the industries,\N它正开始吸引全球各地、各行各业的关注，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.74,0:12:37.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we are doing frontier AI model work in so many different domains.\N因为我们正在众多不同领域开展前沿人工智能模型的研究。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.72,0:12:44.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,The work that we did in proteins, in digital biology, La Proteina, to be able to synthesize and generate proteins.\N我们在蛋白质、数字生物学、La Proteina 方面的工作，能够合成和生成蛋白质。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.08,0:12:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,OpenFold 3 to understand the understand the structure of proteins.\NOpenFold 3 用于理解蛋白质的结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.60,0:12:59.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Evo 2, how to understand and generate multiple proteins, otherwise the beginnings of cellular cellular representation.\NEvo 2 用于理解并生成多种蛋白质，这正是细胞表征的开端。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.67,0:13:02.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Earth 2, AI that understands the laws of physics.\NEarth 2，一种理解物理定律的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.96,0:13:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,The work that we did with FourCastNet, the work that we did with CorrDiff, really revolutionized the way that people are doing weather prediction.\N我们与 FourCastNet 和 CorrDiff 的合作工作，真正革新了人们进行天气预测的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.04,0:13:15.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,NeMo-Megatron, we've now doing groundbreaking work there.\N在 NeMo-Megatron 方面，我们如今正开展开创性的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.13,0:13:23.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first hybrid transformer SSM model that's incredibly fast and therefore can think for a very long time,\N这是首个混合的变换器 SSM 模型，速度极快，因此能长时间思考，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.19,0:13:29.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,or can think very quickly with that for not a very long time, and produce very very smart intelligent answers.\N或在短时间内快速思考，并生成极其智能、精准的答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.83,0:13:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,NeMo-Megatron 3 is groundbreaking work, and you can expect us to deliver other versions of NeMo-Megatron 3 in the near future.\NNeMo-Megatron 3 是开创性的工作，\N未来不久您将看到我们推出 NeMo-Megatron 3 的其他版本。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.88,0:13:45.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cosmos, a frontier open world foundation model, one that understand how the world works.\NCosmos 是一个前沿的开放世界基础模型，能够理解世界运作的原理。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.80,0:13:52.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,GR00T, a humanoid robotic system, articulation, mobility, locomotion, these models,\NGR00T 是一个人形机器人系统，涵盖关节、移动性和运动控制，这些模型，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.60,0:13:59.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,these technologies are now being integrated, and in the each one of these cases open to the world.\N这些技术现在正被整合，且在每种情况下都对世界开放。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.11,0:14:01.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Frontier humanoid robotics models open to the world.\N前沿人形机器人模型对世界开放。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.82,0:14:07.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, today, we're going to talk a little bit about Alpamayo, the work that we've been doing in self-driving cars.\N今天，我们将简要谈谈 Alpamayo，以及我们在自动驾驶汽车方面所开展的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.45,0:14:15.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only do we open source the models, we also open source the data that we used to train those models.\N我们不仅开源模型，还开源了用于训练这些模型的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.60,0:14:22.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because that in that way, only in that way can you truly trust how the models came to be.\N因为只有通过这种方式，您才能真正信任这些模型是如何诞生的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.32,0:14:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,We open source all the models.\N我们开源了所有模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.94,0:14:26.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,We help you make derivatives from them.\N我们帮助您基于这些模型衍生出新的成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.06,0:14:27.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a whole suite of libraries.\N我们提供了一整套工具库。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.98,0:14:34.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,We call them NeMo libraries, physics NeMo libraries, and the Clara NeMo libraries, each bio NeMo libraries.\N我们将它们称为 NeMo 工具库、物理 NeMo 工具库和 \NClara NeMo 工具库，以及各个生物 NeMo 工具库。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.05,0:14:41.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these libraries are life cycle management systems of AIs, so that you could process the data, you could generate data,\N这些库都是AI的生命周期管理系统，让你能够处理数据、生成数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.10,0:14:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,you could train the model, you could create the model, evaluate the model, guardrail the model, all the way to deploying the model.\N训练模型、创建模型、评估模型、为模型设置护栏，直至部署模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.68,0:14:52.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these libraries are incredibly complex, and all of it is open sourced.\N每个库都极其复杂，且全部开源。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.04,0:15:02.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, now, on top of this platform, NVIDIA is a frontier AI model builder, and we build it in a very special way.\N因此，如今在这一平台上，英伟达正成为前沿AI模型的构建者，我们以一种非常特别的方式打造它。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.72,0:15:11.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,We build it completely in the open, so that we can enable every company, every industry, every country to be part of this AI revolution.\N我们完全在开放环境中构建，以便让每家公司、每个行业、每个国家都能参与这场AI革命。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.41,0:15:14.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm incredibly proud of the work that we're doing there.\N我对我们正在做的工作感到无比自豪。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.09,0:15:22.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, if you notice the the charts, the chart shows that our contribution to this industry is bar none,\N实际上，如果你注意到图表，图表显示我们在该行业的贡献是无可争议的，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.61,0:15:26.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you're going to see us, in fact, continue to do that, if not accelerate.\N你将看到我们不仅会持续这样做，甚至可能加速推进。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.64,0:15:28.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,These models are also world-class.\N这些模型同样属于世界级水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.76,0:15:31.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only are they open, they're also top the leaderboards.\N它们不仅开源，还位居排行榜前列。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.97,0:15:33.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an area where we're very proud.\N这是我们非常自豪的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.90,0:15:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They top leaderboards in intelligence.\N它们在智能表现上位居排行榜首位。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.52,0:15:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have uh important models that are understand multi-modality documents, otherwise known as PDFs.\N我们拥有能够理解多模态文档的重要模型，也就是大家所熟知的PDF文件。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.52,0:15:47.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,The most valuable content in the world are captured in PDFs.\N世界上最有价值的内容都保存在PDF文件中。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.70,0:15:54.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, they're it takes artificial intelligence to find out what's inside, interpret what's inside, and help you read it.\N但要发现其中的内容、解读其含义并帮助你阅读，需要借助人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.49,0:15:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, our PDF retrievers, our PDF parsers, are world-class.\N因此，我们的PDF检索器和PDF解析器都是世界级的。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.80,0:16:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our speech recognition models, absolutely world-class.\N我们的语音识别模型，绝对属于世界级水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.04,0:16:12.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our retrieval models, basically search semantic search AI search, the database engine of the modern AI era, world-class.\N我们的检索模型，基本上就是语义搜索、AI搜索，是现代人工智能时代的数据库引擎，堪称世界级。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.26,0:16:15.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're on top of leaderboards constantly.\N所以我们始终稳居各类排行榜前列。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.18,0:16:17.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an area we're very proud of.\N这是我们非常自豪的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.40,0:16:24.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that is in service of your ability to build AI agents.\N所有这些技术都是为了支持你构建AI智能体。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.28,0:16:26.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is really a groundbreaking area of development.\N这确实是一个具有开创性的研发领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.01,0:16:31.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, I first when people when ChatGPT came out, people said, you know,\N你知道，当ChatGPT刚推出时，人们都说，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.13,0:16:36.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh gosh, it it it produced really interesting results, but it hallucinated greatly.\N哇，它确实产生了非常有趣的结果，但幻觉问题很严重。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.12,0:16:40.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason why it hallucinated, of course, it could memorize everything um in the past,\N它产生幻觉的原因当然在于，它无法记住未来所有内容，而只能记住过去的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.70,0:16:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it can't memorize everything in the future in the current.\N它无法记住当前未来的所有内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.52,0:16:45.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it needs to be grounded in research.\N因此，它必须基于研究。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.81,0:16:49.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has to do fundamental research before it answers a question.\N在回答问题之前，它必须进行基础研究。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.04,0:16:52.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,The ability to reason about, do I have to do research?\N能够思考：我是否需要进行研究？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.97,0:16:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do I have to use tools?\N我是否需要使用工具？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.00,0:16:56.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do I break up a problem into steps.\N我该如何将一个问题分解为多个步骤？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.88,0:17:01.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these steps something that that the AI model knows how to do,\N每一步都是AI模型知道如何完成的任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.68,0:17:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and together it is able to compose it into a sequence of steps to perform something it's never done before, it's never been trained to do.\N将这些步骤组合起来，它就能形成一个执行从未做过、也未被训练过任务的步骤序列。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.52,0:17:11.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the wonderful capability of reasoning.\N这正是推理的奇妙能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.69,0:17:16.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could we could be we can encounter a circumstance we've never seen before,\N我们可能会遇到从未见过的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.27,0:17:24.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,and break it down into circumstances and knowledge or rules that we know how to do, because we've experienced it in past.\N但我们可以将其分解为过去经历过、知道如何应对的情境、知识或规则。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.77,0:17:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the ability for AI models now to be able to reason incredibly powerful.\N因此，如今AI模型具备了极其强大的推理能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.20,0:17:34.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reasoning capability of agents opened the doors to all of these different applications.\N智能体的推理能力打开了通向各种应用的大门。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.74,0:17:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,We no longer have to train an AI model to know everything on day one.\N我们不再需要在第一天就让AI模型掌握所有知识。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.33,0:17:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just as we don't have to know everything on day one.\N就像我们不必在第一天就知晓一切一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.64,0:17:47.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That we should be able to in every circumstance reason about how to solve that problem.\N我们应该能够在任何情况下，推理出解决问题的方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.96,0:17:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Large language models has now made this fundamental leap.\N大型语言模型如今实现了这一根本性飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.47,0:17:55.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,The ability to use reinforcement learning and chain of thoughts and you know,\N利用强化学习和思维链等技术，以及
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.39,0:18:02.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,search and planning and all these different techniques and reinforcement learning has made it possible for us to have this basic capability,\N搜索、规划等不同方法，强化学习使我们具备了这种基本能力成为可能，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.60,0:18:05.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it's also now completely open sourced.\N而且现在它已完全开源。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.46,0:18:09.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the thing that's really terrific is another breakthrough that happened.\N但真正令人惊叹的是另一项突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.80,0:18:19.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the first time I saw it was with Eran's Perplexity, Perplexity, the search company, the AI search company, really really innovative company.\N我第一次看到它，是在埃兰的Perplexity公司，那是一家搜索公司，\N也是一家AI搜索公司，真正极具创新精神的企业。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.28,0:18:25.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the first time I realized they were using multiple models at the same time, I thought it was completely genius.\N当我第一次意识到他们同时使用多个模型时，我觉得这简直是天才之举。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.22,0:18:27.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, we would do that.\N当然，我们会这么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.20,0:18:37.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, an AI would also call upon all of the world's great AIs to solve the problem it wants to solve at any part of the reasoning chain.\N当然，AI 在推理链的任何环节，都会调用全球所有优秀AI来解决它想要解决的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.34,0:18:43.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is the reason why AIs are really multi- modal,\N这正是AI真正具备多模态的原因，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.24,0:18:51.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,meaning they understand speech and images and text and videos and 3D graphics and proteins.\N意味着它们能理解语音、图像、文本、视频、三维图形以及蛋白质。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.67,0:18:52.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's multi-modal.\N它是多模态的。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.88,0:19:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's also multi-model, meaning that it should be able to use any model that best fits the task.\N它也是多模型的，意味着它能根据任务需求，灵活使用最适合的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.12,0:19:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is multi-cloud by definition, therefore, because these AI models are sitting in all these different places, and it also is hybrid cloud.\N从定义上讲，它就是多云的，因为这些AI模型分布在各种不同的地方，同时它也是混合云。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.68,0:19:20.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because if you're an enterprise company, or you built a robot, or whatever that device is, sometimes it's at the edge, sometimes a radio cell tower,\N因为你可能是企业公司，或者你开发了一台机器人，或者其他设备，有时它在边缘端，有时在基站塔上，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.28,0:19:29.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe sometimes it's in an enterprise, or maybe it's a place where a hospital where you need to have the the data in real time right next to you.\N有时在企业内部，有时在医院，你需要数据实时地就近处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.10,0:19:36.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whatever those applications are, we know now this is what an AI application looks like in the future.\N无论这些应用是什么，我们现在都清楚，这就是未来AI应用的样子。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.24,0:19:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or another way to think about that, because future applications are built on AIs, this is the basic framework of future applications.\N或者换种方式理解，因为未来应用都是基于AI构建的，这正是未来应用的基本框架。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.72,0:19:53.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,This basic framework, this basic structure of agentic AIs that could do the things that I'm talking about.\N这个基本框架，就是代理式AI的基本结构，它们能够实现我刚才所说的那些功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.86,0:20:01.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is multi-model has now turbocharged AI startups of all kinds.\N这意味着多模型现在已为各类AI初创企业注入了强劲动力。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.40,0:20:06.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now you can also because of the all of the open models and all the tools that we've provided you,\N现在，由于我们提供了所有开源模型和各种工具，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.66,0:20:13.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,you could also customize your AIs to teach your AI skills that nobody else is teaching.\N你还可以定制你的AI，教会它别人从未传授过的技能。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.40,0:20:18.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nobody else is causing their AI to become intelligent or smart in that way.\N没有人会以这种方式让他们的AI变得智能或聪明。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.05,0:20:19.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could do it for yourself.\N你可以自己完成这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.73,0:20:26.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's the work that we do with Nemotron, Nemo, and all of the things that we do with open models is intended to do.\N这正是我们通过Nemotron、Nemo以及所有与开源模型相关的工作所要实现的目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.60,0:20:33.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,You put a smart router in front of it and that router is essentially a manager that decides which one of the task,\N你在前面加一个智能路由器，这个路由器本质上是一个管理者，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.43,0:20:41.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,based on the intention of the prompts that you give it, which one of the models is best fit for that application, for that solving that problem.\N它会根据你输入提示的意图，判断哪个模型最适合该任务、最适合解决该问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.76,0:20:42.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.61,0:20:47.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now when you think about this architecture, what do you have?\N所以当你思考这种架构时，你实际上拥有什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.76,0:20:55.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you think about this architecture, all of a sudden you have an AI that's on the one hand completely customizable by you.\N当你思考这种架构时，突然间你就拥有了一个完全由你定制的AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.20,0:21:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Something that you could teach to do your own very skills for your company.\N你可以教会它完成你公司特有的各种技能。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.12,0:21:02.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Something that's domain secret.\N一种领域机密。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.40,0:21:04.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Something where you have deep domain expertise.\N一种你具备深厚领域专业知识的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.59,0:21:08.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe you've got all of the data that you need to train that AI model.\N或许你已经拥有训练该AI模型所需的所有数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.02,0:21:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the other hand, your AI is always at the frontier by definition.\N另一方面，根据定义，你的AI始终处于前沿。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.72,0:21:21.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're always at the frontier on the one hand, you're always customized on the other hand, and it should just run.\N一方面你始终处于前沿，另一方面你始终是定制化的，而且它应该能直接运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.48,0:21:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we thought we would make the simplest of examples to make it available to you.\N于是我们决定做一个最简单的例子，以便提供给你。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.72,0:21:29.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,This entire framework we call a blueprint.\N我们将整个框架称为蓝图。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.92,0:21:36.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have blueprints that are integrated into enterprise SaaS platforms all over the world and we're really pleased with the progress.\N我们已有集成到全球各地企业SaaS平台中的蓝图，对此我们非常满意。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.63,0:21:44.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,But what we do is show you a a short example of something that anybody can do.\N但我们所做的，是向你展示一个任何人都能完成的简短示例。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.36,0:21:46.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's build a personal assistant.\N我们来打造一个个人助理。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.92,0:21:52.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want it to help me with my calendar, emails, to-do lists, and even keep an eye on my home.\N我希望它能帮我管理日程、邮件、待办事项，甚至还能留意我的家。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.68,0:21:56.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I use Brev to turn my DGX Spark into a personal cloud.\N我用Brev将我的DGX Spark变成个人云。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.76,0:22:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I can use the same interface whether I'm using a cloud GPU or a DGX Spark.\N因此，无论我使用云 GPU 还是 DGX Spark，都可以使用相同的界面。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.76,0:22:08.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I use a frontier model API to easily get started.\N我使用前沿模型 API 来快速上手。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.16,0:22:13.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want it to help me with my emails, so I create an email tool for my agent to call.\N我希望它能帮我处理邮件，所以我为我的智能体创建一个调用的邮件工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.56,0:22:21.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want my emails to stay private, so I'll add an open model that's running locally on the Spark.\N我希望我的邮件保持私密，所以我将在 Spark 上运行一个本地的开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.36,0:22:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now for any job, I want the agent to use the right model for the right task, so I'll use an intent-based model router.\N对于任何任务，我都希望智能体能为正确的工作使用正确的模型，所以我将使用基于意图的模型路由。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.12,0:22:36.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,This way, prompts that need email will stay on my Spark and everything else can call the frontier model.\N这样，需要处理邮件的提示将保留在我的 Spark 上，其他任务则可以调用前沿模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.96,0:22:43.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want my assistant to interact with my world, so I'll hook it up to Hugging Face's Reachy mini robot.\N我希望我的助手能与我的世界互动，所以我将它连接到\NHugging Face 的 Reachy 小型机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.24,0:22:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,My agent controls the head, ears, and camera of the Reachy with tool calls.\N我的智能体通过工具调用控制 Reachy 的头部、耳朵和摄像头。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.16,0:22:52.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to give Reachy a voice and I really like 11 Labs, so I'll hook up their API.\N我想给 Reachy 赋予声音，我特别喜欢 11 Labs，所以我将连接他们的 API。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.96,0:22:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi, I'm Reachy, running on DGX Spark.\N你好，我是 Reachy，运行在 DGX Spark 上。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.16,0:22:59.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey Reachy, what's on my to-do list today?\N嘿，Reachy，我今天的待办事项是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.20,0:23:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Your to-do list today.\N你今天的待办事项。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.00,0:23:07.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Grab groceries, eggs, milk, butter, and send Jensen the new script.\N买点杂货，鸡蛋、牛奶、黄油，然后把新剧本发给黄仁勋。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.28,0:23:09.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's send Jensen that update.\N好的，我们把更新发给黄仁勋吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.24,0:23:11.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tell him we'll have it for him by the end of day.\N告诉他今天之内就能给他。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.84,0:23:12.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Will do.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.41,0:23:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Reachy, there's a sketch too.\NReachy，还有张草图。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.32,0:23:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you turn it into an architectural rendering?\N你能把它转成建筑效果图吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.76,0:23:26.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure.\N当然可以。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.52,0:23:26.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nice.\N很棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.86,0:23:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now make a video and show me around the room.\N现在做个视频，带我看看房间。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.60,0:23:33.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here you go.\N给你。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.16,0:23:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's great.\N太好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.84,0:23:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,With Brev, I can share access to my Spark and Reachy, so I'm going to share it with Anna.\N用 Brev，我可以分享我对 Spark 和 Reachy 的访问权限，所以我打算分享给安娜。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.32,0:23:45.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey Reachy, what's Potato up to?\N嘿，雷奇，土豆在干嘛？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.56,0:23:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,He's on the couch.\N他正躺在沙发上。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.68,0:23:49.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,I remember you don't like this.\N我记得你不喜欢这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.27,0:23:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll tell him to get off.\N我去让他起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.06,0:23:54.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Potato, off the couch.\N土豆，别躺在沙发上。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.36,0:23:58.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,With all the progress in open source, it's incredible to see what you can build.\N随着开源领域的飞速发展，你能构建出的东西真是令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.32,0:24:04.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'd love to see what you create.\N我真想看看你会创造出什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.48,0:24:06.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isn't that incredible?\N这难道不令人惊叹吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.92,0:24:11.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the amazing thing is that is utterly trivial now.\N现在最神奇的是，这一切现在都变得毫无难度。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.92,0:24:14.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is utterly trivial now.\N现在这一切都变得毫无难度。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.52,0:24:20.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And yet just a couple years ago all of that would have been impossible, absolutely unimaginable.\N但就在几年前，这一切都还完全不可能，根本无法想象。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.14,0:24:21.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, this basic framework,\N事实上，这个基础框架，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.79,0:24:30.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,this basic way of building applications using language models that are pretrained and they're proprietary, they're frontier,\N这种利用预训练且专有的前沿语言模型构建应用的基本方式，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.96,0:24:35.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,combine it with customized language models into a agentic framework,\N将其与定制化的语言模型结合，融入代理式框架，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.70,0:24:43.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,a reasoning framework that allows you to access tools and files and maybe even connect to other agents.\N一种推理框架，允许你访问工具、文件，甚至连接其他智能体。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.72,0:24:51.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is basically the architecture of AI applications or applications in the modern age.\N这基本上就是人工智能应用或现代应用的架构。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.56,0:24:55.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the ability for us to create these applications are incredibly fast.\N而我们能够快速创建这些应用的能力极为惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.38,0:25:03.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And notice if you give it this application um information that it's never seen\N注意，如果你提供给它从未见过的应用信息，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.24,0:25:09.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,before or in a structure that has is not represented exactly as you thought,\N或者以一种与你设想不完全一致的结构呈现，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.96,0:25:18.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,it can still reason through it and make its best effort to reason through the data, the information to try to understand how to solve the problem.\N它仍然能够进行推理，并尽最大努力分析数据和信息，尝试理解如何解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.36,0:25:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Artificial intelligence.\N人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.64,0:25:23.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so this basic framework is now being integrated and and everything that I just described,\N好，这种基本框架现在正被整合，我刚才描述的一切都已融入其中，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.86,0:25:28.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have the benefit of working with some of the world's leading enterprise platform companies.\N我们有幸与全球领先的企业平台公司合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.85,0:25:31.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Palantir, for example.\N例如，帕兰提尔。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.64,0:25:38.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I um their their entire AI and data processing platform is being integrated and accelerated by NVIDIA today.\N我们目前正将他们的整个AI和数据处理平台集成并加速，由英伟达实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.56,0:25:44.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,ServiceNow, the world's leading customer service and um employee service platform.\NServiceNow，全球领先的客户服务和员工服务平合。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.19,0:25:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Snowflake, the world's top data platform in the cloud.\NSnowflake，全球领先的云数据平台。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.64,0:25:51.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh incredible work that that uh is being done there.\N那里正在进行的工作令人难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.74,0:25:52.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Code Rabbit.\N代码兔子。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.78,0:25:55.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we're using Code Rabbit all over NVIDIA.\N我们在英伟达的各个地方都在使用代码兔子。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.39,0:26:00.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh CrowdStrike creating AIs to detect, define AI threats.\NCrowdStrike正在创建AI，用于检测和定义AI威胁。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.71,0:26:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh NetApp, their AI their data platform now has NVIDIA semantic AI on top of it and agentic systems on top of it for them to do customer service.\NNetApp，他们的AI数据平台现在已搭载英伟达语义AI，并在其之上构建了代理式系统，用于客户服务。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.32,0:26:18.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the important thing is this, not only is this the way that you develop applications now, this is going to be the user interface of your platform.\N重要的是，这不仅是当前开发应用的方式，更将成为你平台的用户界面。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.96,0:26:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So whether it's Palantir or ServiceNow or Snowflake and many other companies that we're working with, the agentic system is the interface.\N无论是Palantir、ServiceNow、Snowflake，\N还是我们正在合作的众多其他公司，代理式系统就是接口。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.28,0:26:35.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's no longer Excel with a bunch of, you know, squares that you enter enter information into.\N它不再是Excel那种一堆你输入信息的方格。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.09,0:26:38.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's no longer could just command line.\N也许它也不再仅仅是命令行。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.17,0:26:47.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,The any all of that multimodality information is now possible and the way you interact with your platform is much more well,\N现在，多模态信息的任意组合已成为可能，你与平台的交互方式也变得更加自然流畅，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.23,0:26:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you will, simple, like you're interacting with people.\N用你的话说，就像在与人互动一样简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.48,0:26:55.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's enterprise AI being revolutionized by agentic systems.\N因此，代理式系统正在彻底革新企业级 AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.82,0:26:57.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next thing is physical AI.\N下一个方向是物理 AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.85,0:27:00.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an area that you've seen me talk about for several years.\N这是我多年来一直谈论的一个领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.91,0:27:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, we've been working on this for eight years.\N事实上，我们已经在这个方向上深耕了八年。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.72,0:27:04.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,The question is,\N问题在于，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.81,0:27:10.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do you take something that is intelligent inside a computer and interacts\N如何将计算机内部的智能体，从仅通过屏幕和扬声器与你交互，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.60,0:27:17.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,with you with screens and speakers to something that can interact with the world,\N转变为能够与现实世界互动的实体，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.10,0:27:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,meaning it can understand the common sense of how the world works.\N意味着它能理解世界运作的常识。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.12,0:27:23.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Object permanence.\N物体恒存性。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.09,0:27:27.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,If I look away and I look back, that object is still there.\N即使我转过头离开，再回头，那个物体依然存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.16,0:27:28.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um causality.\N但因果关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.11,0:27:29.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,If I push it, it tips over.\N如果我推它，它就会倒下。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.93,0:27:32.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,It understands friction and gravity.\N它理解摩擦力和重力。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.29,0:27:34.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,It understands inertia.\N它理解惯性。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.45,0:27:39.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,That a heavy truck rolling down the road is going to need a little bit more time to stop.\N一辆重型卡车在道路上行驶时，需要更多时间才能停下。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.02,0:27:43.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,That a ball is going to keep on rolling.\N一个球会持续滚动下去。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.68,0:27:49.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,These ideas are common sense to even a little child, but for AI, it's completely unknown.\N这些概念对一个小孩来说都是常识，但对人工智能而言却完全陌生。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.98,0:27:57.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we have to create a system that allows AIs to learn the the common sense of the physical world,\N因此我们必须创建一个系统，让人工智能能够学习物理世界的常识，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.28,0:28:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,learn its laws, but also to be able to, of course,\N学习其规律，同时也能够，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.04,0:28:13.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,learn from data and the data is quite scarce, and to be able to evaluate whether that AI is working, meaning it has to simulate in an environment.\N从数据中学习，而数据却相当稀少，还必须能够评估该人工智能是否在正常工作，\N这意味着它必须在环境中进行模拟。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.12,0:28:18.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,How does an AI know that the the actions that it's performing is consistent with what it should\N人工智能如何知道它所执行的动作与应有的行为一致？
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.00,0:28:24.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,do if it doesn't have the ability to simulate the response of the physical world back on its actions?\N如果它不具备模拟物理世界对其动作反应的能力，又如何得知？
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.50,0:28:31.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The response of its actions is really important to simulate, otherwise there's no way to evaluate it, it's different every time.\N其行为的响应对于模拟至关重要，否则就无法评估，每次的结果都不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.12,0:28:35.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this basic system requires three computers.\N因此这个基础系统需要三台计算机。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.04,0:28:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,One computer, of course, the one that we know that NVIDIA builds for training the AI models.\N一台计算机，当然是我们所知的英伟达用于训练AI模型的那台。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.92,0:28:46.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another computer that we know is to inference the compute inference the models.\N另一台计算机，我们所知的是用于推理的计算推理模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.47,0:28:55.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Inferencing the model is essentially a robotics computer that runs in the car or runs in a robot or runs in a factory, runs anywhere at the edge.\N推理模型本质上是一台机器人计算机，可在汽车、机器人或工厂中运行，也可在任何边缘位置运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.44,0:28:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there has to be another computer that's designed for simulation.\N但必须还有一台专为模拟设计的计算机。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.16,0:29:03.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And simulation is at the heart of almost everything NVIDIA does.\N模拟几乎贯穿了英伟达所做的所有工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.10,0:29:06.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is This is where we are most comfortable.\N这正是我们最擅长的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.60,0:29:12.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And simulation was really the foundations of almost everything that we've done with physical AI.\N模拟确实是我们在物理AI方面所做一切的基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.13,0:29:18.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have three computers and multiple stacks that run on these computers, these libraries to make them useful.\N因此我们有三台计算机，以及运行在这些计算机上的多个软件栈，这些库使它们变得有用。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.81,0:29:24.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Omniverse is our digital twin physically based simulation world.\NOmniverse 是我们的数字孪生物理基础模拟世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.24,0:29:32.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cosmos, as I mentioned earlier, is our foundation model, not a foundation model for language, but a foundation model of the world.\N正如我之前提到的，Cosmos 是我们的基础模型，不是语言的基础模型，而是世界的基座模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.64,0:29:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's also aligned with language.\N而且它也与语言对齐。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.36,0:29:37.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could say something like, you know, what's happening to the ball?\N你可以说类似这样的话，你知道，球正在发生什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.03,0:29:40.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they'll tell you the ball's rolling down the street.\N他们会告诉你球正在沿着街道滚动。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.64,0:29:44.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so a world foundation model and then, of course, the robotics models.\N然后是一个世界基础模型，当然还有机器人模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.72,0:29:46.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have two of them.\N我们有两个。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.07,0:29:48.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of them is called GR00T.\N其中一个叫 GR00T。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.44,0:29:51.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other one's called Alpamayo that I'm going to tell you about.\N另一个叫 Alpamayo，我接下来会跟你们讲到。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.28,0:29:57.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the one of the most important things that we have to do with physical AI is to create the data to train the AI in the first place.\N我们在物理 AI 上必须做的最重要的一件事，就是创建用于训练 AI 的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:57.60,0:29:59.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where does that data come from?\N这些数据从哪里来？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.76,0:30:09.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Rather than instead of having languages because we created a bunch of text that are what we consider ground truth that the AI can learn from,\N不是像我们创建大量文本那样，那些文本是我们认为的真实情况，AI 可以从中学习，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.60,0:30:12.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do we teach an AI the ground truth of physics?\N我们该如何教 AI 真实的物理规律？
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.33,0:30:21.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are lots and lots of videos, lots and lots of videos, but hardly enough to capture the diversity and the type of interactions that we need.\N虽然有大量视频，大量视频，但几乎不足以捕捉我们所需的多样性和交互类型。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.48,0:30:31.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this is where great minds came together and transformed what used to be compute into data.\N于是，这里就是伟大思想汇聚之地，将原本的计算转变为数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.92,0:30:38.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, using synthetic data generation that is grounded and conditioned by the laws of physics,\N现在，利用基于物理定律生成的合成数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.03,0:30:49.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,grounded and conditioned by ground truth, we can now selectively cleverly generate data that we can then use to train the AI.\N基于真实数据进行约束和引导，我们可以有选择地、巧妙地生成数据，进而用于训练人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.59,0:31:01.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, for example, what comes into this AI, this Cosmos AI world model on the left on over here, is the output of a traffic simulator.\N举个例子，输入到左侧这个宇宙AI世界模型中的，是交通模拟器的输出结果。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.24,0:31:06.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, this traffic simulator is hardly enough for an AI to learn from.\N然而，仅靠这个交通模拟器，人工智能很难从中学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.68,0:31:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can take this, put it into a Cosmos Foundation model,\N我们可以将这些数据输入到宇宙基础模型中，
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.44,0:31:19.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,and generate surround video that is physically based and physically plausible that the AI can now learn from.\N生成基于物理、符合物理规律的环绕视频，让人工智能能够从中学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.95,0:31:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And there are so many examples of this.\N这样的例子还有很多。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.12,0:31:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let me show you what Cosmos can do.\N让我来展示一下宇宙模型的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.16,0:31:32.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Chat GPT moment for physical AI is nearly here.\N物理AI的ChatGPT时刻即将来临。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.80,0:31:34.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the challenge is clear.\N但挑战显而易见。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.47,0:31:39.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The physical world is diverse and unpredictable.\N物理世界是多样且不可预测的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.12,0:31:45.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Collecting real-world training data is slow and costly, and it's never enough.\N收集真实世界的训练数据既缓慢又昂贵，而且永远都不够。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:45.16,0:31:48.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The answer is synthetic data.\N答案是合成数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.60,0:31:56.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It starts with NVIDIA Cosmos, an open frontier world foundation model for physical AI.\N它始于英伟达 Cosmos，一个面向物理 AI 的开放前沿世界基础模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.76,0:32:04.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pre-trained on internet-scale video, real driving and robotics data, and 3D simulation.\N基于互联网规模的视频、真实驾驶和机器人数据，以及 3D 模拟进行预训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.84,0:32:13.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cosmos learned a unified representation of the world, able to align language, images, 3D, and action.\NCosmos 学习了世界的统一表示，能够对齐语言、图像、3D 和动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.88,0:32:21.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It performs physical AI skills like generation, reasoning, and trajectory prediction.\N它能执行物理 AI 技能，如生成、推理和轨迹预测。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.20,0:32:27.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,From a single image, Cosmos generates realistic video.\N仅凭一张图像，Cosmos 就能生成逼真的视频。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.40,0:32:33.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,From 3D scene descriptions, physically coherent motion.\N根据 3D 场景描述，生成物理上一致的运动。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.64,0:32:39.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,From driving telemetry and sensor logs, surround video.\N根据驾驶遥测数据和传感器日志，生成环绕视频。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.76,0:32:45.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,From planning simulators, multi-camera environments.\N根据规划模拟器，生成多相机环境。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.40,0:32:51.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or from scenario prompts, it brings edge cases to life.\N或者根据场景提示，让边缘案例栩栩如生。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.20,0:32:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Developers can run interactive closed-loop simulations in Cosmos.\N开发者可以在 Cosmos 中运行交互式的闭环模拟。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.92,0:33:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,When actions are made, the world responds.\N当采取行动时，世界会作出回应。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.96,0:33:03.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cosmos reasons.\N宇宙模型进行推理。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.56,0:33:13.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It analyzes edge scenarios, breaks them down into familiar physical interactions, and reasons about what could happen next.\N它分析边缘场景，将其分解为熟悉的物理交互，并推理接下来可能发生的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.84,0:33:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cosmos turns compute into data, training AVs for the long tail,\N宇宙模型将算力转化为数据，用于训练自动驾驶汽车应对长尾场景，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.32,0:33:30.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,and robots how to adapt for every scenario.\N以及让机器人学会适应各种情境。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.04,0:33:33.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know, it's incredible.\N我知道，这太不可思议了。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.04,0:33:39.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cosmos is the world's leading foundation model, world foundation model.\N宇宙模型是全球领先的通用基础模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.30,0:33:43.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's been downloaded millions of times, used all over the world.\N它已被下载数百万次，全球各地都在使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.44,0:33:47.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Getting world getting the world ready for this new era of physical AI.\N正在让世界为这个物理 AI 的新时代做好准备。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.37,0:33:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use it ourselves as well.\N我们自己也在使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.72,0:33:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use it ourselves to create our self-driving car.\N我们用它来打造自己的自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.04,0:34:00.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Using it for scenario generation and using it for evaluation,\N用于场景生成，也用于评估。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.28,0:34:10.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,we could have something that allows us to effectively travel billions, trillions of miles, but doing it inside a computer.\N我们可以拥有某种技术，让我们在计算机内部实现数十亿、数万亿英里的有效旅行。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.16,0:34:12.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've made enormous progress.\N我们已经取得了巨大的进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.25,0:34:23.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we're announcing Alpamayo, the world's first thinking, reasoning autonomous vehicle AI.\N今天，我们宣布推出Alpamayo，这是世界上首个具备思考与推理能力的自动驾驶AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.76,0:34:31.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alpamayo is trained end to end, literally from camera in to actuation out.\NAlpamayo采用端到端训练，真正实现了从摄像头输入到执行输出的完整流程。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.08,0:34:37.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The camera in, lots and lots of miles that are driven by itself using human demonstration,\N摄像头输入的数据，来自它自身通过人类示范驾驶的大量里程。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.48,0:34:41.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we have lots and lots of miles that are generated by Cosmos.\N此外，我们还通过宇宙系统生成了海量的里程数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.60,0:34:50.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,In addition to that, hundreds of thousands of examples are labeled very, very carefully so that we could teach the car how to drive.\N除此之外，还有数十万条经过极其精细标注的样本，用于教会汽车如何驾驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.59,0:34:53.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alpamayo does something that's really special.\NAlpamayo做了一件非常特别的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.96,0:35:00.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only does it take sensor input and activates steering wheel, brakes,\N它不仅接收传感器输入并控制方向盘、刹车和油门，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.47,0:35:07.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,and and acceleration, it also reasons about what action it's about to take.\N还会推理自己即将采取的动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.75,0:35:15.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It tells you what action it's going to take, the reasons by which it came about that action, and then of course the trajectory.\N它会告诉你它将采取什么动作，做出该决定的原因，以及相应的行驶轨迹。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.88,0:35:27.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these are coupled directly and trained very specifically by a large combination of human trained and as well as Cosmos generated data.\N所有这些都直接耦合，并通过大量人类训练数据与宇宙系统生成数据的组合，进行了专门训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.28,0:35:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The result of it is just really incredible.\N结果令人惊叹不已。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.00,0:35:38.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only does your car drive as you would expect it to drive, and it drives so naturally because it learned directly from human demonstrators,\N你的汽车不仅像你预期的那样行驶，而且行驶得如此自然，因为它直接从人类示范者那里学到了驾驶方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.64,0:35:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,but in every single scenario when it comes up to the scenario, it reasons about it,\N但在每一个场景中，它都会对此进行推理，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.92,0:35:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,tells you what it's going to do, and it reasons about what it's what it's about to do.\N它会告诉你它接下来要做什么，并且会推理自己即将要做的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:46.84,0:35:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the reason why this is so important is because of the long tail of driving.\N现在，这之所以如此重要，是因为驾驶中的长尾效应。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.84,0:35:59.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,There it's impossible for us to simply collect every single possible scenario for everything that could ever happen\N那种情况下，我们根本不可能收集所有可能发生的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.23,0:36:06.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,in every single country and every single circumstance that's possibly ever going to happen for all of population.\N在所有可能发生的国家和所有可能的情境下，适用于全人类。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.12,0:36:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, it is very unlikely it's very likely that every scenario,\N然而，几乎不可能的是，每种情景都极有可能发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.88,0:36:18.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,if decomposed into a whole bunch of other smaller scenarios, are quite normal for you to understand.\N如果分解成许多其他较小的情景，对你来说理解起来就相当正常了。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.82,0:36:25.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, these long tails will be decomposed into quite normal circumstances that the car knows how to deal with.\N因此，这些长尾场景将被分解为车辆熟悉并能应对的常规情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.78,0:36:27.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,It just needs to reason about it.\N它只需要进行推理即可。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.35,0:36:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, let's take a look.\N那么，让我们来看一看。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.60,0:36:31.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everything you're about to see is one shot.\N你即将看到的一切都是单次拍摄完成的。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.28,0:36:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a no hands.\N这是完全无人驾驶的。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.68,0:36:40.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Routing to your destination.\N正在为您导航至目的地。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.36,0:38:17.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Buckle\N系好
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.06,0:39:12.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,up.\N安全带。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.32,0:39:15.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You\N您
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.80,0:39:20.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,have\N已到达。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.16,0:39:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,arrived.\N我们八年前就开始研发自动驾驶汽车，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.00,0:39:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We started working on self-driving cars 8 years ago,\N原因在于我们很早就意识到，深度学习和人工智能将彻底重塑整个
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.24,0:39:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the reason for that is because we reasoned early on that deep learning and artificial intelligence was going to reinvent the entire\N计算领域。如果我们想要理解如何自主导航，并引领行业迈向这一新未来，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.72,0:39:48.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,computing And if we were ever going to understand how to navigate ourselves and how to guide the industry towards this new future,\N就必须精通构建整个技术栈的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.40,0:39:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have to get good at building the entire stack.\N我们必须擅长构建整套技术栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.32,0:39:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, as I mentioned earlier, AI is a five-layered cake.\N嗯，正如我之前提到的，AI 是一个五层蛋糕。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.24,0:39:58.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,The lowest layer is land, power, and shell.\N最底层是土地、电力和厂房。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.64,0:40:01.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the case of robotics, the lowest layer is the car.\N在机器人领域，最底层就是汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.64,0:40:03.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next layer above it is chips.\N再往上一层是芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.96,0:40:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPUs, networking chips, CPUs, all that kind of stuff.\NGPU、网络芯片、CPU 等各类芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.20,0:40:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next layer above that is the infrastructure.\N再往上一层是基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.36,0:40:18.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That infrastructure, in this particular case, as I mentioned with physical AI, is Omniverse and Cosmos.\N在这个特定情况下，正如我之前提到的物理 AI，基础设施就是 Omniverse 和 Cosmos。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:18.84,0:40:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then above that are the models.\N然后是模型层。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:21.88,0:40:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in the case of the models above that I just shown you, the model here is called Alpha Miao.\N就在我刚才展示的那些模型中，这个模型叫做 Alpha Miao。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.52,0:40:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Alpha Miao today is open-sourced.\N而 Alpha Miao 目前已经开源。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.52,0:40:39.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We This incredible body of work, it took several thousand people.\N我们完成了这项令人惊叹的工作，投入了数千人。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:39.48,0:40:41.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our AV team is several thousand people.\N我们的自动驾驶团队就有数千人。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.41,0:40:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just to put in perspective, our partner uh Ola, I think Ola is here in the audience somewhere.\N为了让大家有个更清晰的认识，我们的合作伙伴奥拉，我想奥拉就在观众席的某个地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.08,0:40:54.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Mercedes agreed to partner with us 5 years ago to go make all of this possible.\N梅赛德斯-奔驰五年前同意与我们合作，让这一切成为可能。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.81,0:40:59.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We imagine that someday a billion cars on the road will all be autonomous.\N我们设想，有一天道路上将有十亿辆汽车全部实现自动驾驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.62,0:41:05.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could either have it be a robo-taxi that you're you're you're orchestrating and and renting from somebody,\N你可以选择使用自动驾驶出租车，由你协调并从他人那里租用，
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.97,0:41:10.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,or you could own it and it's driving for you driving by itself, or you could decide to drive for yourself.\N或者你可以拥有它，让它自动为你驾驶，或者你也可以自己驾驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.84,0:41:14.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, but every single car will have autonomous vehicle capability.\N因此，每一辆汽车都将具备自动驾驶能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.22,0:41:16.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single car will be AI-powered.\N每一辆汽车都将由 AI 驱动。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:16.52,0:41:23.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the the the model layer in this case is Alpha Miao, and the application above that is the Mercedes-Benz.\N在这个案例中，模型层是 Alpha Miao，其上的应用层是梅赛德斯-奔驰。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.96,0:41:24.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:41:24.57,0:41:31.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so this entire stack is our first NVIDIA first entire stack endeavor.\N因此，整个技术栈是我们首次 NVIDIA 全栈式努力的成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:31.40,0:41:40.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've been working on it for this entire time, and we're so happy that the first AV car from NVIDIA is going to be on the road in Q1,\N我们一直在为此投入，非常高兴的是，英伟达的第一辆自动驾驶汽车将在第一季度上路，
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.69,0:41:48.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then it goes Europe in Q2 here in the United States in Q1, then Europe in Q2, and I think it's Asia in Q3 and Q4.\N然后第一季度在美国上市，第二季度进入欧洲，我认为第三季度和第四季度将覆盖亚洲。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.56,0:41:55.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the powerful thing is that we're going to keep on updating it with next next versions of Alpha Miao and versions after that.\N最重要的是，我们将持续用 Alpha Miao 的下一代版本以及后续版本来更新它。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.84,0:42:03.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's no question in my mind now that this is going to be one of the largest robotics industries, and I'm so happy that we worked on it.\N我现在毫不怀疑，这将成为规模最大的机器人产业之一，我很高兴我们参与了这项工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:03.14,0:42:09.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it taught us enormous amount about how to help the rest of the world build robotic systems.\N它让我们学到了大量关于如何帮助世界其他地区构建机器人系统的经验。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.64,0:42:14.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,That deep understanding and knowing how to build it ourselves, building the entire infrastructure ourselves,\N这种深入的理解，以及我们自己构建整个基础设施的能力，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.78,0:42:18.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,and knowing what kind of chips a robotic system would would need.\N还有我们清楚地知道机器人系统需要什么样的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.70,0:42:24.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,In this particular particular case, dual Orions, the next generation dual Thors,\N在这个特定案例中，是双 Orion，下一代双 Thor，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.56,0:42:32.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,these processors are designed for robotic systems, and was designed for the safe highest level of safety capability.\N这些处理器专为机器人系统设计，具备最高级别的安全保障能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.46,0:42:38.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,This car just got rated it just went to production.\N这辆车刚刚完成评级，已进入量产阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:38.44,0:42:41.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Mercedes-Benz CLA was just rated\N梅赛德斯-奔驰 CLA 刚刚获得
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.78,0:42:50.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,by NCAP the world's safest car.\NNCAP 评级，被评为全球最安全的汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.60,0:42:59.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is the only system that I know that has every single line of code, the chip, the system, every line of code safety certified.\N我所知道的唯一一个系统，其所有代码、芯片、系统都经过了安全认证。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.67,0:43:08.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The entire model system is based on a sensors are diverse and redundant, and so is the self-driving car stack.\N整个模型系统基于多样且冗余的传感器，自动驾驶系统也是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.28,0:43:13.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Alpha Miao stack is trained end to end and has incredible skills.\NAlpha Miao 系统是端到端训练的，具备惊人的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.32,0:43:19.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, nobody knows until you drive it forever that it's going to be perfectly safe.\N但只有当你持续驾驶它时，才能确定它是否真正安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.28,0:43:26.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the we the way we guardrail that is with another software stack, an entire AV stack underneath.\N因此，我们通过另一个软件栈——一个完整的自动驾驶底层系统——来实现防护。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.40,0:43:32.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,That entire AV stack is built to be fully traceable, and it's taken us some 5 years to build that,\N这整个自动驾驶系统都设计为完全可追溯，我们花了大约5年时间才完成它的构建，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.43,0:43:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,some 6 7 years actually, to build that second stack.\N实际上是花了大约6到7年时间才完成第二个栈的构建。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:35.64,0:43:42.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,These two software stacks are mirroring each other, and then we have a policy and safety evaluated decide,\N这两个软件栈相互镜像，然后我们通过策略和安全评估来判断，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:42.36,0:43:47.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,is this something that I'm very confident and can reason about driving very safely?\N这是否是我非常有信心、能够合理判断为安全驾驶的情况？
Dialogue: 0,0:43:47.26,0:43:49.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,If so, I'm going to have Alpha Miao do it.\N如果是，我就会让 Alpha Miao 执行该操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.20,0:43:53.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it's a circumstance that I'm not very confident in and the safety um\N如果是我不太有信心、安全策略评估认为存在风险的情况，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.56,0:43:58.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,policy evaluator decide that we're going to go back to what's a very a simpler,\N我们将返回到一个更简单、更安全的防护系统，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:58.21,0:44:02.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,safer guardrail system, then it goes back to the classical AV stack.\N然后系统会切换回传统的自动驾驶栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:02.28,0:44:09.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're the only car in the world with both of these AV stacks running, and all safety systems should have diversity and redundancy.\N我们是全球唯一一辆同时运行这两种自动驾驶栈的汽车，所有安全系统都应具备多样性和冗余性。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.36,0:44:16.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, our vision is that someday every single car, every single truck will be autonomous, and we've been working towards that future.\N我们的愿景是，有朝一日每一辆汽车、每一辆卡车都将实现自动驾驶，我们一直在为此未来而努力。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.12,0:44:20.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,This entire stack is vertically integrated, of course, in the case of Mercedes-Benz.\N当然，梅赛德斯-奔驰的整个技术栈都是垂直整合的。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.84,0:44:22.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We built the entire stack together.\N我们共同构建了整个技术栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:22.40,0:44:23.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to deploy the car.\N我们将部署这辆汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.24,0:44:24.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to operate the stack.\N我们将运营这个技术栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.21,0:44:26.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to maintain the stack for as long as we shall live.\N我们将长期维护这个技术栈，直到我们生命的终结。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:27.04,0:44:36.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, like everything else we do as a company, we build the entire stack, but the entire stack is open for the ecosystem.\N然而，就像我们公司所做的其他一切一样，我们构建了整个技术栈，但整个技术栈对生态系统是开放的。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.24,0:44:44.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And these the ecosystem working with us to build L4 and robo-taxis is expanding and it's going everywhere.\N与我们合作开发 L4 级自动驾驶和自动驾驶出租车的生态系统正在不断扩展，并已遍及全球。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.80,0:44:48.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,I fully expect this to be Well, this is already a giant business for us.\N我完全相信，这已经是我们的一项巨大业务。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.34,0:44:54.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a giant business for us because they use it for training our training data, processing data, and training their models.\N这对我们来说是一项巨大业务，因为他们用它来训练我们的训练数据、处理数据，并训练他们的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.36,0:44:56.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,They use it for synthetic data generation.\N他们用它来生成合成数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.72,0:45:04.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,In some cases, in some car in some companies, they build pretty much just build the computers, the chips that are inside the car.\N在某些情况下，某些汽车公司几乎只负责制造汽车内部的计算机和芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.45,0:45:06.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And some companies work with us full stack.\N有些公司与我们进行全栈合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:06.35,0:45:09.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some companies work with us some partial part of that.\N有些公司只与我们合作其中部分环节。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.42,0:45:09.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.89,0:45:12.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it doesn't matter how much you decide to use.\N所以，你决定使用多少完全无关紧要。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.86,0:45:16.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, my only request is you use a little bit of video wherever you can.\N我唯一的请求是，只要有可能，尽量多用一些视频。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.64,0:45:19.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the entire thing is open.\N而整个系统都是开源的。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:19.52,0:45:27.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, this is going to be the first large-scale mainstream um AI physical AI market.\N现在，这将是首个大规模主流的物理 AI 市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.80,0:45:31.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is now, I think we can all agree, fully here.\N而且我认为，我们都可以认同，它现在已经真正到来。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:31.46,0:45:40.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this inflection point of going from not autonomous vehicles to autonomous vehicles is probably happening right about this time.\N从非自动驾驶车辆转向自动驾驶车辆的转折点，很可能就发生在现在这个时刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.20,0:45:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,In in the next 10 years, I'm fairly certain a very, very large percentage of the world's cars will be autonomous or highly autonomous.\N在接下来的十年里，我相当确信，世界上绝大多数汽车将实现自动驾驶或高度自动驾驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:48.84,0:45:53.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,But this is this basic technique that I just described in using the three computers,\N但正如我刚才描述的，使用三台计算机、合成数据生成和仿真的基本技术，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.35,0:45:59.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,using the synthetic data generation and simulation, applies to every form of robotic systems.\N适用于所有类型的机器人系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.65,0:46:03.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It could be a robot that is just an articulator, a manipulator.\N它可能只是一个关节执行器或操作臂。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.40,0:46:04.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's a mobile robot.\N也许它是一个移动机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.94,0:46:07.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's a fully humanoid robot.\N也许它是一个完全人形的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.56,0:46:15.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the next journey the next era for robotic systems is going to be, you know, robots.\N因此，机器人系统下一个旅程、下一个时代将是，你知道的，机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.47,0:46:18.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And these robots are going to come in all kinds of different sizes.\N这些机器人将有各种各样的尺寸。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.29,0:46:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And I invited some friends.\N我还邀请了一些朋友。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:21.08,0:46:23.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey guys.\N嘿，伙计们。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.60,0:46:24.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hurry up.\N快点。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.76,0:46:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did you tell R2-D2 you're going to be here?\N你告诉R2-D2你会来吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.00,0:46:30.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did you?\N你说了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:30.52,0:46:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And C-3PO?\N还有C-3PO呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.60,0:46:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.98,0:46:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, come here.\N好了，过来这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.36,0:46:38.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Before Now, one of the things that one of the things that's really You have Jetsons.\N以前，有一件事特别有意思，就是你们有杰森一家。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.01,0:46:42.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have little Jetson computers inside them.\N它们内部有小型杰森电脑。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.16,0:46:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're trained inside Omniverse.\N它们是在 Omniverse 里训练的。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:44.88,0:46:46.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how about this?\N那这个呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.28,0:46:51.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's show everybody the simulator that you were that you guys learn how to how to be robots in.\N我们来给大家看看你们学习如何成为机器人的那个模拟器。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.00,0:46:54.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want You guys want to look at that?\N你们想看看这个吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.20,0:46:55.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's look at that.\N好，我们来看看。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.24,0:46:55.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Run it,\N运行它，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.56,0:47:57.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,please.\N拜托了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:57.80,0:48:02.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isn't that amazing?\N难道不神奇吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.40,0:48:04.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's how you learn to be a robot.\N这就是你们学习如何成为机器人的方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.45,0:48:06.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You did it all inside Omniverse.\N你所有的工作都是在 Omniverse 里完成的。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.88,0:48:09.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the robot simulator is called Isaac.\N机器人模拟器叫做 Isaac。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:09.72,0:48:11.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isaac Sim and Isaac Lab.\NIsaac Sim 和 Isaac 实验室。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:11.16,0:48:17.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And anybody who wants to build a robot, you know, nobody could Nobody's going to be as cute as you.\N任何想制造机器人的人都知道，没人能比你们更可爱了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.40,0:48:22.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,But now we have all Look at all these Look at all these friends that we have building robots.\N但现在我们有了所有这些朋友，都在一起制造机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.58,0:48:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have We're building big ones.\N我们正在制造大型机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.94,0:48:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,No Like I said, nobody's as cute as you guys are, but we have Neurobot, and we have Agibot over there.\N就像我说的，没人能比你们更可爱，但我们还有 Neurobot，还有那边的 Agibot。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.76,0:48:32.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we have LG over here.\N我们这边还有 LG。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:32.78,0:48:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,They just announced a new robot.\N他们刚刚宣布了一款新机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.36,0:48:38.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Caterpillar, they've got the largest robots ever.\N卡特彼勒公司，他们拥有迄今为止最大的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.56,0:48:41.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,That one delivers food to your house.\N那个机器人会把食物送到你家。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.22,0:48:42.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's connected to Uber Eats.\N它连接了 Uber Eats。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.86,0:48:45.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that Surf robot, I love those guys.\N那个 Surf 机器人，我超喜欢那些家伙的。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.64,0:48:49.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Agility, Boston Dynamics, incredible.\N通用性，波士顿动力，太厉害了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.90,0:48:51.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,You got surgical robots.\N你有手术机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.43,0:48:55.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,You got manipulator robots from Franka.\N你有来自 Franka 的机械臂机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:55.24,0:48:59.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You got Universal Robotics robot, incredible number of different robots.\N你还有 Universal Robotics 机器人，各种不同的机器人数量惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.52,0:49:01.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this is the next chapter.\N所以，这是下一个篇章。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:01.73,0:49:07.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to talk a lot more about robotics in the future, but it's not just about the robots in the end.\N未来我们会更多地谈论机器人，但最终这不仅仅关乎机器人本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:07.42,0:49:09.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know everything's about you guys.\N我知道一切都关乎你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.21,0:49:10.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's about getting there.\N这关乎如何抵达那里。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.58,0:49:14.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of the one of the most important industries in the world that will\N世界上最重要的产业之一，将被物理 AI 和 AI 物理彻底改变。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.75,0:49:22.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,be revolutionized by physical AI and AI physics is the industry that started all of us.\N这正是我们所有人起步的那个产业。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.64,0:49:27.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,At NVIDIA, it wouldn't be possible if not for the companies that I'm about to talk to.\N在英伟达，如果没有我接下来要提到的那些公司，这一切都不可能实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.42,0:49:31.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm so happy that all of them, starting with Cadence,\N我非常高兴，所有这些公司，从楷登电子开始，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.30,0:49:37.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,is going to accelerate everything Cadence CUDA X integrated into all of their simulations and solvers.\N都将加速集成楷登电子 CUDA-X 的所有仿真和求解器。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.47,0:49:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've got NVIDIA physical physical AIs that they're going to use for for different physical plants and plant simulations.\N他们拥有英伟达的物理 AI，将用于不同的物理工厂和工厂仿真。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.72,0:49:49.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,You got AI physics being integrated into these systems.\N人工智能物理正在被整合进这些系统中。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.25,0:49:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, whether it's an EDA or SDA and in the future robotic systems, we're going to have basically the same technology that made you guys possible.\N无论是 EDA 或 SDA，还是未来的机器人系统，我们都将拥有使你们成为可能的相同技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.80,0:50:02.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now completely revolutionize these design stacks.\N现在将彻底革新这些设计架构。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.74,0:50:11.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Synopsys, without Synopsys You know, Synopsys and Cadence are completely completely indispensable in the world of chip design.\N没有楷登电子和新思科技，你根本无法想象芯片设计世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.91,0:50:18.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Synopsys is uh leads in uh in logic design and and IP.\N新思科技在逻辑设计和 IP 领域处于领先地位。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.49,0:50:25.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh in the case of Cadence, they lead physical design, the place and route, uh and emulation and verification.\N楷登电子则在物理设计、布局布线、仿真和验证方面处于领先地位。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:25.16,0:50:27.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cadence is incredible at emulation and verification.\N楷登电子在仿真和验证方面非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.71,0:50:32.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Both of them are moving into the world of system design and system simulation.\N两者都在向系统设计和系统仿真领域迈进。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:32.59,0:50:38.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, in the future we're going to design your chips inside Cadence and inside Synopsys.\N未来，我们将通过楷登电子和新思科技来设计你们的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.84,0:50:45.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to design your systems and emulate the whole thing and simulate everything inside these tools.\N我们将设计你的系统，并在这些工具内部完整模拟和仿真所有内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.10,0:50:46.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's your future.\N这就是你的未来。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.24,0:50:50.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to give Yeah, you're going to be born inside these inside these platforms.\N我们将让你诞生于这些平台之中。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.87,0:50:52.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pretty amazing, right?\N非常惊人，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.51,0:50:55.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we're so happy that we're working with these these industries.\N因此，我们非常高兴能与这些行业合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.91,0:51:00.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just as we've integrated NVIDIA into Palantir and ServiceNow,\N就像我们已将英伟达集成到 Palantir 和 ServiceNow 一样，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:00.11,0:51:08.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're integrating NVIDIA into the most computationally intensive simulation industries, Synopsys and Cadence.\N我们现在正将英伟达集成到计算密集型仿真行业中最核心的领域，即 Synopsys 和 Cadence。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:08.16,0:51:12.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And today we're announcing that Siemens is also doing the same thing.\N而今天，我们宣布西门子也正在做同样的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.20,0:51:21.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to integrate CUDA X physical AI, agentic AI, Nemo, Nemotron deeply integrated into the world of Siemens.\N我们将把 CUDA-X 物理 AI、代理式 AI、\NNemo 和 Nemotron 深度集成到西门子的生态系统中。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:21.25,0:51:23.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is this.\N原因就在于此。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:24.00,0:51:29.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,First, we design the chips and all of it in the future will be accelerated NVIDIA.\N首先，我们将使用这些工具设计芯片，而未来所有内容都将由英伟达加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:29.44,0:51:31.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going to be very happy about that.\N你会对此感到非常满意。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:31.19,0:51:36.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to have agentic chip designers and system designers working with us,\N我们将拥有代理式芯片设计师和系统设计师与我们协作，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.73,0:51:42.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,helping us do design just as we have agentic software engineers helping our software engineers code today.\N就像如今我们有代理式软件工程师协助软件工程师编写代码一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.94,0:51:46.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we'll have agentic chip designers and system designers.\N因此，我们将拥有代理式芯片设计师和系统设计师。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:46.52,0:51:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to create you inside this.\N我们将在这之中为你创造。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.72,0:51:52.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But then, we have to build you.\N但随后，我们必须建造你。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.40,0:51:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have to build the plants, the factories that make manufacture you.\N我们必须建造生产你的工厂和车间。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.60,0:52:02.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have to design the manufacturing lines that assemble all of you.\N我们必须设计组装你们所有人的制造产线。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.48,0:52:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And these manufacturing plants are going to be essentially gigantic robots.\N这些制造工厂本质上将是巨大的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.08,0:52:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredible, isn't that right?\N难以置信，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.64,0:52:11.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know.\N我知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.64,0:52:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know.\N我知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.64,0:52:15.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you're going to be designed in a computer.\N所以，你将在计算机中被设计出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:15.56,0:52:17.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going to be made in a computer.\N你将在计算机中被制造出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.88,0:52:26.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going to be tested and evaluated in a computer long before long before you have to spend any time dealing with gravity.\N你将在计算机中接受测试和评估，远在你需要面对重力之前。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.84,0:52:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know.\N我知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:29.04,0:52:31.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you know how to deal with gravity?\N你知道如何应对重力吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:31.68,0:52:34.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you jump?\N你能跳吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.24,0:52:46.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you jump?\N你能跳吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.20,0:52:46.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.62,0:52:47.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:47.38,0:52:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Don't show off.\N别炫耀。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.48,0:52:49.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:49.30,0:52:51.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so this So,\N所以，所以这个，
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.49,0:52:58.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,now the industry the industry that made NVIDIA possible where I'm just so happy that the now the technology\N现在，那个让英伟达成为可能的产业，我真是太高兴了，现在这项技术
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.83,0:53:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we're creating is at a level of sophistication and capability that we can now help them revolutionize their industry.\N我们正在创造的技术，其复杂程度和能力水平已经高到足以帮助他们彻底革新整个行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.68,0:53:12.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, what started with with with them, we now have the opportunity to go back and and help them revolutionize theirs.\N因此，当初由他们开启的事业，如今我们有机会反哺回去，帮助他们彻底革新自己的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.70,0:53:16.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's take a look at the stuff that we're going to do with Siemens.\N我们来看一下接下来与西门子合作的项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.68,0:53:18.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Come on.\N来吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.52,0:53:26.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Breakthroughs in physical AI are letting AI move from screens to our physical world.\N物理 AI 的突破正让 AI 从屏幕走向现实世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:26.84,0:53:36.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just in time as the world builds factories of every kind for chips, computers, life-saving drugs, and AI.\N正好赶上全球各地都在建设各类工厂，包括芯片、计算机、救命药物以及 AI 工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:36.20,0:53:45.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,As the global labor shortage worsens, we need automation powered by physical AI and robotics more than ever.\N随着全球劳动力短缺日益严重，我们比以往任何时候都更需要由物理 AI 和机器人驱动的自动化。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:45.64,0:53:53.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,This, where AI meets the world's largest physical industries, is the foundation of NVIDIA and Siemens partnership.\N这正是 AI 与全球最大物理产业交汇之处，也是英伟达与西门子合作的基石。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.32,0:53:58.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,For nearly two centuries, Siemens has built the world's industries.\N近两个世纪以来，西门子一直在构建全球的工业体系。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:58.52,0:54:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, it is reinventing it for the age of AI.\N如今，它正为 AI 时代重新定义工业。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:03.36,0:54:10.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Siemens is integrating NVIDIA CUDA X libraries AI models and Omniverse\N西门子正在将其 EDA、CAE 和数字孪生工具及平台整合英\N伟达的 CUDA-X 库、AI 模型和 Omniverse。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.96,0:54:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,into its portfolio of EDA CAE and digital twin tools and platforms.\N使其成为其产品组合的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.16,0:54:27.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Together, we're bringing physical AI to the full industrial life cycle.\N我们正共同将物理 AI 带入整个工业生命周期。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.24,0:54:36.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,From design and simulation to production and operations.\N从设计和仿真，到生产与运营。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:36.20,0:54:39.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We stand at the beginning of a new industrial revolution.\N我们正站在一场新工业革命的起点。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.96,0:54:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The age of physical AI built by NVIDIA and Siemens for the next age of industries.\N这是英伟达与西门子共同打造的物理 AI 时代，为下一代工业而生。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:50.48,0:54:54.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredible, right, guys?\N难以置信，对吧，各位？
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.44,0:54:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you think?\N你们怎么看？
Dialogue: 0,0:54:55.92,0:54:56.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:56.31,0:54:56.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll hang on tight.\N我会抓紧的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.01,0:54:58.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just hang on tight.\N只管抓紧就行。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:58.16,0:55:08.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so this is you know, if you look at look at the world's models there's no question OpenAI is the the leading token generator today.\N所以，你看，如果观察世界模型，毫无疑问，目前 OpenAI 是领先的词元生成者。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:08.92,0:55:12.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,More to more OpenAI tokens are generated than just about anything else.\N生成的 OpenAI 词元数量，远超其他任何事物。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.66,0:55:16.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second largest group the second largest probably open models.\N第二大群体，可能是第二大的开放模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.89,0:55:21.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And my guess is that over time, because there are so many companies, so many researchers,\N我猜随着时间推移，由于公司众多、研究人员众多，
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.37,0:55:27.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,so many different types of domains and modalities that open source models will be by far the largest.\N不同领域和模态也多种多样，开源模型将远远超过其他模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:27.56,0:55:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's talk about somebody really special.\N我们来聊一位特别的人。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:29.68,0:55:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You guys want to do that?\N你们想试试吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.76,0:55:34.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's talk about Vera Rubin.\N我们来聊一聊Vera Rubin。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:34.28,0:55:36.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Vera Rubin Yeah, go ahead.\NVera Rubin，好，你先说。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.56,0:55:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,She's an American astronomer.\N她是一位美国天文学家。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.60,0:55:50.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,She was the first to observe She noticed that the tails of the galaxies were moving about as fast as the center of the galaxies.\N她是第一个观察到星系尾部的运动速度与星系中心几乎相同的人。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:50.08,0:55:52.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, I know it makes no sense.\N我知道这听起来毫无道理。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.52,0:55:53.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,It makes no sense.\N这确实毫无道理。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.58,0:55:56.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Newtonian physics would say, just like the solar system,\N牛顿物理学会说，就像太阳系一样，
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.95,0:56:04.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,the planets further away from the sun is circling the sun slower than the planets closer to the sun.\N离太阳越远的行星，绕太阳公转的速度越慢，而离太阳越近的行星则越快。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.52,0:56:10.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And therefore, it makes no sense that this happens unless there's invisible bodies,\N因此，除非存在看不见的物体，否则这种情况毫无意义，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.01,0:56:18.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,we call them she discovered dark body dark matter, um that occupies space even though we don't see it.\N我们称其为她发现的暗体暗物质，它占据空间，尽管我们看不见它。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.93,0:56:25.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, Vera Rubin is the person that we named our next computer after.\N所以，我们把下一台计算机命名为Vera Rubin。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.16,0:56:27.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isn't that a good idea?\N这不是个好主意吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.48,0:56:31.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know.\N我知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.16,0:56:31.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.54,0:56:35.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Vera Rubin is designed to address this fundamental challenge that we have.\NVera Rubin的设计正是为了解决我们面临的这一根本性挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.88,0:56:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,The amount of computation necessary for AI is skyrocketing.\N人工智能所需的计算量正在急剧上升。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.80,0:56:43.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,The demand for NVIDIA GPUs is skyrocketing.\N英伟达GPU的需求正在急剧上升。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:43.47,0:56:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's skyrocketing because models are increasing by a factor of 10 an order of a magnitude every single year.\N这是因为模型每年都在提升一个数量级，也就是十倍增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.52,0:56:56.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And not to mention, as I mentioned, 01's introduction was an inflection point for AI.\N更不用说，正如我提到的，01的发布是人工智能的一个转折点。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.92,0:57:03.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Instead of a one-shot answer, inference is now a thinking process.\N与一次性回答不同，推理现在变成了一种思考过程。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:03.06,0:57:12.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in order to teach the AI how to think, reinforcement learning and very significant computation was introduced into post-training.\N为了教会AI如何思考，我们在后训练阶段引入了强化学习和大量计算。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:12.60,0:57:21.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It wasn't no long It's no longer supervised fine-tuning or otherwise known as imitation learning or supervision training.\N这不再是监督微调，也不再是模仿学习或监督训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.24,0:57:29.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,You now have reinforcement learning, essentially the computer trial trying different iterations itself, learning how to perform a task.\N现在你有了强化学习，本质上是计算机自己尝试不同的迭代，学习如何完成任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.51,0:57:38.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,The amount of computation for pre pre-training, for post-training, for test time scaling has exploded as a result of that.\N由于这一变化，预训练、后训练以及推理阶段的计算量都急剧增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.39,0:57:45.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now every single inference that we do, instead of just one shot, the number of tokens you could just see the AIs think, which we appreciate.\N现在我们每次推理，不再只是单次尝试，而是能看到AI思考的词元数量，这一点我们非常欣赏。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:45.87,0:57:48.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,The longer it thinks, often times it produces a better answer.\N通常思考时间越长，AI给出的答案质量越高。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.71,0:57:55.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, test time scaling causes the number of tokens to be generated increase by 5x every single year.\N因此，推理阶段的缩放使生成的词元数量每年增加5倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.64,0:58:01.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not to mention meanwhile, the race is on for AI.\N更不用说，AI竞赛正在激烈进行。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:01.08,0:58:02.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody's trying to get to the next level.\N每个人都在努力迈向下一个层级。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.82,0:58:04.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody's trying to get to the next frontier.\N每个人都在努力突破下一个前沿。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.62,0:58:15.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every time they get to the next frontier the last generation AI tokens, the cost starts to starts to decline about a factor of 10x every year.\N每当他们抵达下一个前沿，上一代AI的词元成本每年就会下降约10倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.39,0:58:18.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,The 10x decline every year is actually telling you something different.\N每年10倍的下降实际上在告诉你一些不同的信息。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.03,0:58:21.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's saying that the race is so intense.\N它在说这场竞赛如此激烈。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:21.44,0:58:26.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody's trying to get to the next level and somebody is getting to the next level.\N每个人都在努力迈向下一个层级，而有人确实已经到达了下一个层级。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.66,0:58:29.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, therefore all of it is a computing problem.\N因此，所有这一切本质上都是一个计算问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.78,0:58:34.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The faster you compute, the sooner you can get to the next level of the next frontier.\N你计算得越快，就越能早日抵达下一个前沿。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.28,0:58:37.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these things are simultaneously happening at the same time.\N所有这些事情正在同时发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:37.78,0:58:46.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we decided that we have to advance the state of the art of computation every single year.\N所以我们决定，必须每年都在计算技术上实现突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.10,0:58:48.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not one year left behind.\N不能有一年落后。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:48.27,0:58:53.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, we've been shipping GB200s year and a half ago.\N现在，我们已经提前一年半开始出货 GB200。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:53.77,0:58:58.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right now, we're in full-scale manufacturing of GB300.\N目前，我们正在全力生产 GB300。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:58.76,0:59:05.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if Vera Rubin is going to be in time for this year, it must be in production by now.\N如果 Vera Rubin 要赶上今年的进度，那它现在就必须已投入生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:05.77,0:59:15.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, today I can tell you that Vera Rubin is in full production.\N所以今天我可以告诉你们，Vera Rubin 已经进入全面生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:15.84,0:59:17.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,You guys want to take a look at Vera Rubin?\N你们想看看 Vera Rubin 吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:17.77,0:59:18.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.80,0:59:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Come on.\N来吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:19.64,0:59:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Play it, please.\N请播放。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:24.16,0:59:29.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Vera Rubin arrives just in time for the next frontier of AI.\NVera Rubin正好赶上了 AI 的下一个前沿。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:29.76,0:59:32.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This This the story of how we built it.\N这就是我们如何打造它的故事。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:32.56,0:59:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The architecture, a system of six chips engineered to work as one, born from extreme co-design.\N架构由六颗芯片组成，经过极致协同设计，协同工作如同一体。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.60,0:59:45.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It begins with Vera, a custom-designed CPU, double the performance of the previous generation.\N起始于Vera，这是一款定制设计的 CPU，性能是上一代的两倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:45.44,0:59:46.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the Rubin GPU.\N以及Rubin GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:46.88,0:59:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Vera and Rubin are co-designed from the start to bidirectionally and coherently share data faster and with lower latency.\NVera和Rubin从一开始就协同设计，双向且一致地共享数据，速度更快，延迟更低。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.24,1:00:04.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then, 17,000 components come together on a Vera Rubin compute board.\N然后，17,000 个组件在Vera Rubin计算板上汇聚。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:04.28,1:00:14.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,High-speed robots place components with micron precision before the Vera CPU and two Rubin GPUs complete the assembly.\N高速机器人以微米级精度放置组件，随后Vera CPU 和两块Rubin GPU 完成组装。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:14.12,1:00:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Capable of delivering 100 petaflops of AI, five times that of its predecessor.\N能够提供 100 petaflops 的 AI 算力，是前代产品的五倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:21.88,1:00:24.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI needs data fast.\NAI 需要快速获取数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:25.04,1:00:33.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,ConnectX-9 delivers 1.6 terabits per second of scale-out bandwidth to each GPU.\NConnectX-9 为每个 GPU 提供 1.6 太比特每秒的横向扩展带宽。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:33.64,1:00:41.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,BlueField-4 DPU offloads storage and security, so compute stays fully focused on AI.\NBlueField-4 DPU 负责卸载存储和安全任务，使计算资源能完全专注于 AI。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:41.40,1:00:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Vera Rubin compute tray, completely redesigned with no cables, hoses, or fans.\NVera Rubin 计算托盘，经过全新设计，完全无电缆、无管道、无风扇。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:48.28,1:00:57.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Featuring a BlueField-4 DPU, eight ConnectX-9 NICs, two Vera CPUs, and four Rubin GPUs.\N配备 BlueField-4 DPU、八个 ConnectX-9 网卡、\N两个 Vera CPU 和四个 Rubin GPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.48,1:01:02.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,The compute building block of the Vera Rubin AI supercomputer.\NVera Rubin AI 超级计算机的计算积木单元。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:02.20,1:01:07.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Next, the sixth-generation NVLink switch.\N接下来是第六代 NVLink 交换机。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.16,1:01:18.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Moving more data than the global internet, connecting 18 compute nodes, scaling up to 72 Rubin GPUs operating as one.\N传输的数据量超过全球互联网，连接 18 个计算节点，\N可扩展至 72 个 Rubin GPU 作为一体运行。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:18.44,1:01:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then, Spectrum-X Ethernet photonics.\N然后是 Spectrum-X 以太网光子学技术。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:24.16,1:01:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,The world's first Ethernet switch with 512 lanes and 200 gigabit capable co-\N全球首款具备 512 通道且支持 200 吉比特的以太网交换机，采用共封装光学技术。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:30.08,1:01:36.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,packaged optics scale out thousands of racks into an AI factory.\N将数千个机架横向扩展为一个 AI 工厂。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:36.40,1:01:45.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,15,000 engineer years since design began, the first Vera Rubin NVL72 rack comes online.\N自设计启动以来已历时 15,000 人年，首个 Vera Rubin NVL72 机架正式上线。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.12,1:01:51.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Six breakthrough chips, 18 compute trays, nine NVLink switch trays,\N六款突破性芯片，18个计算机架，九个NVLink交换机机架，
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.27,1:01:57.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,220 trillion transistors, weighing nearly two tons.\N2200亿个晶体管，重量接近两吨。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:58.04,1:02:02.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,One giant leap to the next frontier of AI.\N向AI的下一个前沿迈出巨大一步。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:03.00,1:02:09.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Rubin is here.\NRubin来了。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:09.84,1:02:14.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you guys think?\N你们觉得怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,1:02:14.64,1:02:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a Rubin pod.\N这是一个Rubin模块。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:17.68,1:02:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,1,152 GPUs in 16 racks.\N16个机架内共搭载1152块GPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:23.00,1:02:27.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of the racks, as you know, has uh 72 Rubins.\N每个机架，如你们所知，包含72个Rubin。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:27.79,1:02:33.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of the Rubins is two actual GPU dies connected together.\N每个Rubin由两个实际的GPU晶片连接而成。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:33.55,1:02:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to show it to you.\N我现在就给你们展示一下。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:35.16,1:02:42.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, there are several things that, well, I'll tell you later.\N但还有几件事，稍后再告诉你们。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:42.40,1:02:44.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we designed six different chips.\N我们设计了六种不同的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:44.40,1:02:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,First of all, we have a rule inside our company, and it's a good rule.\N首先，我们公司内部有一条规则，这是一条很好的规则。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.24,1:02:53.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,No new generation should have more than one or two chips change.\N新一代产品不应有超过一到两个芯片的变更。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.48,1:02:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the problem is this.\N但问题是这样。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:55.40,1:03:01.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you could see, we were describing the total number of transistors in each one of the chips that were being described,\N如你所见，我们描述的是每个芯片中晶体管的总数，
Dialogue: 0,1:03:01.22,1:03:04.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we know that Moore's law has largely slowed.\N而我们知道，摩尔定律已大幅放缓。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:04.07,1:03:13.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the number of transistors we can get year after year after year can't possibly keep up with the 10 times larger models.\N因此，我们每年所能获得的晶体管数量，根本无法跟上模型规模扩大十倍的节奏。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:13.96,1:03:19.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can't possibly keep up with five times per year more tokens generated.\N它根本无法跟上每年生成词元数量增加五倍的速度。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.14,1:03:26.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can't possibly keep up with the fact that cost decline of the tokens are going to be so aggressive.\N它根本无法跟上词元成本下降将变得如此激进的事实。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:26.40,1:03:34.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is impossible to keep up with those kind of rates for the industry to continue to advance unless we deployed aggressive,\N若不采用激进的、极端的协同设计，整个行业根本无法持续前进。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:34.90,1:03:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,extreme co-design, basically innovating across all of the chips, across the entire stack, all at the same time.\N也就是说，我们必须在所有芯片上同时创新，贯穿整个技术栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:42.92,1:03:49.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which is the reason why we decided that this generation, we had no choice but to design every chip over again.\N这正是我们决定这一代产品必须重新设计每一颗芯片的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:49.43,1:03:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, every single chip that we were describing just now can be a press conference in all in itself,\N现在，我们刚才提到的每一颗芯片，本身都足以开一场发布会。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:54.72,1:03:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and there's an entire company whose product dedicated to doing that back in the old days.\N还有一家公司，其产品专门致力于实现这一点，这在多年前就已经开始了。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.44,1:04:04.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of them are completely revolutionary and the best of its kind.\N它们每一个都完全具有革命性，是同类产品中的佼佼者。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.88,1:04:07.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Vera CPU, I'm so proud of it.\N我对这款 Vera CPU 非常自豪。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:07.25,1:04:15.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,In a power-constrained world, Grace CPU is two times the performance in a power-constrained world.\N在功耗受限的世界里，Grace CPU 的性能提升了两倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:15.39,1:04:20.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's twice the performance per watt of the world's most advanced CPUs.\N它的每瓦性能是当今最先进 CPU 的两倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:20.56,1:04:22.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Its data rate is insane.\N它的数据传输速率惊人。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:22.32,1:04:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was designed to process supercomputers, and Grace was an incredible CPU.\N它是专为处理超级计算机而设计的，Grace 是一款非凡的 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.84,1:04:36.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, Vera increases the single-threaded performance, increases the capacity of the memory, increases everything just dramatically.\N现在，Vera 显著提升了单线程性能，大幅增加了内存容量，各方面都实现了飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:37.04,1:04:38.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a giant chip.\N这是一颗巨大的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:38.71,1:04:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the Vera CPU.\N这是 Vera CPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:41.12,1:04:43.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is one CPU.\N这是一颗 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:43.64,1:04:50.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is connected to the Rubin GPU.\N它连接到了 Rubin GPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:50.40,1:04:53.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Look at that thing.\N看看那个东西。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:53.24,1:04:54.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a giant chip.\N这是一块巨大的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:54.18,1:04:58.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the thing that's really special, and I'll I'll go through these.\N真正特别的是这个，我来一一说明。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:58.40,1:05:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to take three hands, I think, four hands to do this.\N我觉得得用三只手，可能得四只手才能完成。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:02.12,1:05:03.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so this is the Vera the Vera CPU.\N好，这是Vera CPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.88,1:05:08.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got 88 CPU cores, and the CPU cores are designed to be multithreaded.\N它有 88 个 CPU 核心，这些核心设计为多线程。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:08.60,1:05:18.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the multithreaded nature of of Vera was designed so that each one of the 176 threads could get its full full performance.\N但Vera的多线程特性是这样设计的：176 个线程中的每一个都能获得完整的性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:18.06,1:05:22.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's essentially as if there's 176 cores, but only 88 physical cores.\N所以本质上，就像是有 176 个核心，但实际上只有 88 个物理核心。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:22.75,1:05:28.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, these cores were designed in in using a technology called spatial multithreading.\N这些核心是使用一种叫空间多线程的技术设计的。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:28.27,1:05:30.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the IO performance is incredible.\N但它的 I/O 性能惊人。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:30.27,1:05:31.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the Rubin GPU.\N这是Rubin GPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:31.95,1:05:35.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's 5x Blackwell in floating performance.\N它的浮点性能是黑尔威的 5 倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.46,1:05:37.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the important thing is go to the bottom line.\N但最重要的是，要看到根本所在。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:37.72,1:05:41.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,The bottom line, it's only 1.6 times the number of transistors of Blackwell.\N底线是，它只有黑尔威尔芯片晶体管数量的1.6倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:41.63,1:05:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,That kind of tells you something about the the levels of semiconductor physics today.\N这其实说明了当今半导体物理的水平。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:46.72,1:05:54.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we don't do extreme co-design at the level of basically every single chip across the entire system,\N如果我们不在整个系统中对几乎每一个芯片都进行极致的协同设计，
Dialogue: 0,1:05:54.32,1:06:02.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,how is it possible we deliver performance levels that is, you know, at best 1.6 times each year?\N那么我们怎么可能实现每年性能提升最多仅1.6倍的情况？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:02.36,1:06:04.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because that's the total number of transistors you have.\N因为那正是你拥有的晶体管总数。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:04.53,1:06:09.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And even if you were to have a little bit more um performance per transistor, say 25%,\N即使每个晶体管的性能稍有提升，比如25%，
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.04,1:06:14.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're this impossible to get 100% yield out of the number of transistors you get.\N你也几乎不可能从这些晶体管中获得100%的良率。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.21,1:06:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, 1.6x kind of puts a ceiling on how far performance can go each year unless you do something extreme, and we call it extreme co-design.\N因此，1.6倍的提升实际上设定了每年性能提升的上限，除非你采取极端措施，我们称之为极致协同设计。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:23.40,1:06:30.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, one of the things that one of the things that we did, and it was a great invention, is called NVFP4 Tensor Core.\N我们做的一件事，是一项伟大的发明，叫做NVFP4张量核心。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.40,1:06:37.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,The transformer engine inside our chip is not just a four-bit floating-point number somehow that we put into the data path.\N我们芯片内部的变换器引擎，并不只是简单地将一个4位浮点数放入数据路径。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.46,1:06:45.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is an entire processor, a processing unit that understands how to dynamically, adaptively,\N它是一个完整的处理器，一个能动态、自适应地理解
Dialogue: 0,1:06:45.79,1:06:53.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,adjust its precision and structure to deal with different levels of the transformer so that you can achieve higher\N调整其精度和结构，以应对变换器的不同层级，从而实现更高的性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:53.05,1:07:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,throughput wherever it's possible to lose precision and to go back to the highest possible precision wherever you need to.\N在任何可能丢失精度的地方，都要尽可能恢复到最高精度，以满足你的需求。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:00.64,1:07:07.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,That ability to dynamically do that, you can't do this in software because, obviously, it's just running too fast.\N这种动态处理能力，你无法通过软件实现，因为显然它的运行速度太快了。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:07.95,1:07:12.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you have to be able to do it adaptively inside the processor.\N因此，你必须能够在处理器内部动态地完成它。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:12.48,1:07:18.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what an NVFP4 When somebody says FP4 or FP8, it almost means nothing to us.\N这就是 NVFP4。当有人说 FP4 或 FP8 时，对我们来说几乎毫无意义。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:18.41,1:07:24.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because it's the Tensor Core structure and all of the algorithms that makes makes it work.\N原因在于其张量核心架构以及所有使它运行的算法。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:24.47,1:07:26.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,NVFP4, we've published papers on this already.\NNVFP4，我们已经发表过相关论文了。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:26.98,1:07:33.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,The precision that the the level of throughput and precision is able to retain is in com- and completely incredible.\N其吞吐量和精度的保持水平之精准，堪称不可思议。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:33.07,1:07:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is groundbreaking work.\N这是开创性的研究。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:34.88,1:07:41.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would not be surprised if the industry would like us to make this format and this structure an industry standard in the future.\N我一点都不奇怪，业界未来会希望我们把这种格式和结构定为行业标准。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:41.26,1:07:43.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is completely revolutionary.\N这完全是革命性的。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:43.10,1:07:52.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is how we were able to deliver such a gigantic step up in performance even though we only have 1.6 times the number of transistors.\N尽管晶体管数量仅增加了1.6倍，我们仍能实现性能的巨大飞跃，这就是原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:52.96,1:07:58.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, once you have a great processing node, and this is the processor node,\N现在，当你拥有了一个出色的处理节点，也就是这个处理器节点，
Dialogue: 0,1:07:58.56,1:08:07.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,and inside, so this is this is, for example, here, let me do this.\N而在内部，比如这里，让我来演示一下。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:07.12,1:08:11.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is This is wow, super heavy.\N这个东西，哇，非常重。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:11.16,1:08:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to be a CEO in really good shape to do this job.\N你得是位身体状况极佳的CEO才能胜任这份工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:17.44,1:08:18.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:18.06,1:08:19.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:19.18,1:08:24.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this thing is I'm going to guess this is probably,\N所以，这个东西我猜大概是，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.48,1:08:31.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know, couple of hundred pounds.\N我也不确定，大概有几百磅。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:32.04,1:08:34.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought that was funny too.\N我也觉得这挺搞笑的。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:34.96,1:08:35.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Come on.\N来吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:35.95,1:08:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It could have been.\N也有可能。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:38.16,1:08:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody's going, "No, I don't think so."\N大家都在说：“不，我不这么认为。”
Dialogue: 0,1:08:41.28,1:08:41.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.01,1:08:43.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so look at this.\N所以，看看这个。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:43.39,1:08:44.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the last one.\N这是最后一个。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.81,1:08:49.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We revolutionized the entire MGX chassis.\N我们彻底革新了整个 MGX 机箱。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.44,1:08:53.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This node, 43 cables.\N这个节点，有 43 根电缆。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.64,1:08:55.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Zero cables.\N一根电缆都没有。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.36,1:08:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Six tubes.\N六根管道。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.16,1:09:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Z- Just two of them here.\NZ——这里只有两根。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:01.52,1:09:05.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It takes two hours to assemble this.\N组装这个需要两个小时。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:06.00,1:09:08.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you're lucky, it takes two hours.\N如果你运气好，也需要两个小时。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:08.72,1:09:10.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course, you're probably going to assemble it wrong.\N当然，你很可能组装错了。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:10.65,1:09:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going to have to retest it, test it, reassemble it.\N你得重新测试，测试，再重新组装。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:13.76,1:09:21.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the assembly process is incredibly complicated, and it it was understandable as one of our first supercomputers that's deconstructed in this way.\N所以，组装过程非常复杂，作为我们第一台超计算机之一，以这种方式拆解是完全可以理解的。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.04,1:09:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,This, from two hours to five minutes.\N从两小时缩短到五分钟。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:31.52,1:09:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,80% liquid cooled.\N80% 采用液冷。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:34.00,1:09:36.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,100% liquid cooled.\N100% 采用液冷。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:37.04,1:09:40.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, really, really a breakthrough.\N是的，这确实是一次真正的重大突破。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:40.68,1:09:49.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so so this is the new compute chassis and what connects all of these to the top of rack switches,\N好，这是新的计算机箱，它连接所有设备到机架顶部的交换机。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:49.24,1:09:52.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,the east-west traffic, is called a Spectrum-X NIC.\N东西向流量由 Spectrum-X 网络接口卡处理。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:52.11,1:09:54.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the world's best NIC.\N这是全球最好的网卡。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:54.84,1:10:00.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unquestionably NVIDIA's Mellanox, the acquisition Mellanox that joined us a long time ago now.\N毫无疑问，是英伟达收购的 Mellanox，那家公司很久以前就加入我们了。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:00.40,1:10:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um this their networking technology for high-performance computing is the world's best bar none.\N他们的高性能计算网络技术，毫无疑问是全球最佳。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:05.68,1:10:11.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,The algorithms, the chip design, all of the interconnects, all the software stacks that we're running on top of it,\N算法、芯片设计、所有互连技术，以及我们运行在其上的所有软件栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:11.16,1:10:15.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,their RDMA, absolutely, absolutely bar none, the world's best.\N他们的 RDMA 技术，毫无疑问，绝对是全球最佳。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:15.18,1:10:20.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now it has the ability to do programmable RDMA and data path accelerator so that our partners\N现在它具备了可编程 RDMA 和数据路径加速功能，使我们的合作伙伴
Dialogue: 0,1:10:20.85,1:10:25.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,like AI labs could create their own algorithms for how they want to move data around the system.\N例如 AI 实验室，能够根据自身需求设计数据在系统中传输的专属算法。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:26.00,1:10:29.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But this is completely world world class ConnectX.\N但这是真正世界级的 ConnectX。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:29.40,1:10:35.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,ConnectX-9 and the Vera CPU were co-designed and we never revealed it not never never released\NConnectX-9 和 Vera CPU 是协同设计的，我们从未透露过，也从未发布过
Dialogue: 0,1:10:35.91,1:10:43.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,it until CX-9 came along because we we co-designed it for a new type of processor.\N直到 ConnectX-9 出现才公开，因为我们是为一种新型处理器协同设计的。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:43.40,1:10:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, ConnectX-9 or CX-8 and Spectrum-X revolutionized how Ethernet was done for artificial intelligence.\N你知道，ConnectX-9 或 CX-8 以及\NSpectrum-X 彻底改变了人工智能领域的以太网实现方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:52.32,1:10:57.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ethernet traffic for AI is much, much more intense, requires much lower latency.\N人工智能的以太网流量强度高得多，对延迟要求也低得多。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:57.69,1:11:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,The the instantaneous surge of traffic is unlike anything Ethernet sees and so we created Spectrum-X which is AI Ethernet.\N这种瞬时流量激增是传统以太网从未见过的，因此我们开发了 Spectrum-X，即 AI 以太网。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:07.96,1:11:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,2 years ago we announced Spectrum-X.\N两年前我们宣布了 Spectrum-X。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:10.80,1:11:15.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,NVIDIA today is the largest networking company the world has ever seen.\N如今英伟达是全球有史以来最大的网络公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:15.36,1:11:19.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's been so successful and used in so many different installations.\N它如此成功，已被广泛应用于各种不同场景。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:20.02,1:11:22.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is just sweeping the AI landscape.\N它正在彻底席卷人工智能领域。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:23.03,1:11:31.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,The performance is incredible, especially when you have a 200 megawatt data center or if you have a gigawatt data center,\N性能非常惊人，尤其是当你拥有一个200兆瓦的数据中心，或者一个吉瓦级的数据中心时，
Dialogue: 0,1:11:31.18,1:11:32.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,these are billions of dollars.\N这些都是数十亿美元的投入。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:32.64,1:11:35.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's say a gigawatt data center is 50 billion dollars.\N假设一个吉瓦级的数据中心价值500亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:35.91,1:11:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,If the networking performance allows you to deliver an extra 10%\N如果网络性能能让你额外提升10%的效率，
Dialogue: 0,1:11:43.00,1:11:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the case of Spectrum-X delivering 25% higher throughput is not uncommon.\N在Spectrum-X的情况下，实现25%的吞吐量提升并不罕见。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:48.16,1:11:52.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it were to just deliver 10%, that's worth 5 billion dollars.\N如果仅仅提升10%，价值就高达50亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:52.05,1:11:54.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,The networking is completely free.\N网络性能是完全免费的。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:54.76,1:11:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which is the reason why well everybody uses Spectrum-X.\N这正是为什么所有人都在使用Spectrum-X的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:59.00,1:12:00.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just an incredible thing.\N这实在令人难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:00.66,1:12:06.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now we're going to invent a new type a new type of data processing.\N现在我们将发明一种全新的数据处理方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:06.44,1:12:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so Spectrum-X is for east-west traffic.\N因此，Spectrum-X适用于东西向流量。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:09.88,1:12:12.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,We now have a new processor called BlueField-4.\N我们现在推出了一款新型处理器，名为BlueField-4。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:12.37,1:12:17.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,BlueField-4 allows us to take a large large very large data center isolate\NBlueField-4 让我们能够将大型数据中心划分为多个独立部分
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.59,1:12:21.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,different parts of it so that different users could use different parts of it,\N以便不同用户可以使用其中的不同部分，
Dialogue: 0,1:12:21.09,1:12:24.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,make sure that everything could be virtualized if they decide to be virtualized.\N确保如果他们决定进行虚拟化，所有内容都可以被虚拟化。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:24.56,1:12:32.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you offload a lot of the virtualization software, the security software, the networking software for your north-south traffic.\N因此，你可以将大量虚拟化软件、安全软件以及南北向流量的网络软件卸载。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.94,1:12:37.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so BlueField-4 comes standard with every single one of these compute nodes.\N所以 BlueField-4 会作为每个计算节点的标准配置。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:37.84,1:12:42.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,BlueField-4 has a second application I'm going to talk about in just a second.\NBlueField-4 还有一个我接下来要讲的第二个应用场景。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:42.16,1:12:45.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a revolutionary processor and I'm so excited about it.\N这是一款革命性的处理器，我对此非常激动。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:45.17,1:12:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the NVLink 6 switch and it's right here.\N这是 NVLink 6 交换机，就在这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:52.64,1:13:00.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the this switch this switch here, there's four of them inside the NVLink switch here.\N这个交换机，就是这里的这个交换机，NVLink 交换机内部有四个这样的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:00.24,1:13:04.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these switch chips has the fastest 30s in history.\N每个交换芯片都拥有史上最快的 30 秒性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.56,1:13:07.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,The world is barely getting to 200 gigabits.\N全球目前才刚刚达到 200 吉比特的水平。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:07.23,1:13:11.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is 400 gigabits per second switch.\N这是一个每秒 400 吉比特的交换机。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:11.16,1:13:18.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why this is so important is so that we could have every single GPU talk to every other GPU at exactly the same time.\N这样做的重要性在于，我们可以让每一块GPU同时与其它所有GPU进行通信。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:18.88,1:13:25.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,This switch this switch on the backplane of one of these racks enables\N这个机架背板上的开关 enables
Dialogue: 0,1:13:25.96,1:13:33.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,us to move the equivalent of twice the amount of the global internet data.\N我们能够传输相当于全球互联网数据量两倍的数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:33.12,1:13:37.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of the world's internet data at twice the speed.\N全球互联网数据以两倍的速度传输。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:37.08,1:13:43.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,You take the cross-sectional bandwidth of the entire planet's internet, it's about 100 terabytes per second.\N将全球互联网的横截带宽加总，大约为每秒100太字节。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:43.59,1:13:45.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is 240 terabytes per second.\N这个速度达到了每秒240太字节。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:45.95,1:13:47.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that puts it in perspective.\N这样一来，大家就能清楚地理解其意义了。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:47.94,1:13:53.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is so that every single GPU can work with every single other GPU at exactly the same time.\N这样做的目的就是让每一块GPU都能在同一时刻与其他所有GPU协同工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:53.40,1:13:54.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:13:54.44,1:13:58.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then on top of that on top of that.\N在此基础上，再进一步。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:58.60,1:14:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so this is one rack.\N好，这是其中一个机架。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:00.48,1:14:01.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is one rack.\N这是一个机架。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:01.34,1:14:03.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of the racks, as you could see,\N每个机架，如你所见，
Dialogue: 0,1:14:03.34,1:14:14.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,the number of transistors in this one rack is 1.7 times Yeah, could you do this for me?\N这个机架的晶体管数量是通常的1.7倍，嗯，你能帮我做一下吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.58,1:14:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is it's usually about 2 tons but today is 2 and 1/2 tons\N所以通常重量约为2吨，但今天是2.5吨
Dialogue: 0,1:14:20.60,1:14:26.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,because um when they shipped it they forgot to drain the water out of it.\N因为他们发货时忘了把里面的水排掉。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:27.00,1:14:33.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we we shipped a lot of water from California.\N所以我们从加利福尼亚运出了大量水。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:33.64,1:14:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you hear it squealing?\N你能听到它在吱吱作响吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:14:35.84,1:14:41.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, when you're rotating 2 and 1/2 tons you're going to squeal a little.\N你知道，当你转动2.5吨重的东西时，会有点吱吱作响。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:41.42,1:14:46.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So behind behind this are the NVLink spines.\N在这后面是NVLink的主干。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:46.64,1:14:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically 2 miles of copper cables.\N基本上是2英里的铜缆。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:49.60,1:14:53.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Copper is the best conductor we know and these are all shielded copper cables,\N铜是我们所知导电性最好的材料，这些全部是屏蔽铜缆，
Dialogue: 0,1:14:53.64,1:14:58.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,structured copper cables, the most the world's ever used in computing systems ever.\N结构化铜缆，是全球计算系统中使用过的最多数量。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:58.96,1:15:08.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and our 30s drive the copper cables from the top of the rack all the way to the bottom of the rack at 400 gigabits per second.\N而我们的30系列从机架顶部一路驱动铜缆到底部，速率高达每秒400吉比特。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:08.72,1:15:09.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's incredible.\N难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:10.01,1:15:14.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this has 2 miles of total copper cables, 5,000 copper cables.\N这里总共有两英里长的铜缆，共计五千根铜缆。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:14.78,1:15:18.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this makes the NVLink spine possible.\N这使得 NVLink 脊柱成为可能。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:19.02,1:15:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the revolution that that really started the MGX system.\N这才是真正开启 MGX 系统革命的关键。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:23.00,1:15:29.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we we decided that we would create an industry standard system so that the entire ecosystem,\N现在我们决定打造一个行业标准系统，让整个生态系统，
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.04,1:15:34.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,all of our supply chain could standardize on these components.\N我们的所有供应链都能统一采用这些组件。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:34.49,1:15:45.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's some 80 thousand different components that make up this these MGX systems and it's a total waste if we were to change it every single year.\N这些 MGX 系统由大约八万个不同组件构成，如果每年都要更换，那将是巨大的浪费。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:45.24,1:15:49.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single major computer company from Foxconn to Quanta to Wistron, you know,\N从富士康到广达再到纬创，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,1:15:49.81,1:15:56.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,the list goes on and on and on to HP and Dell and Lenovo, everybody knows how to build these systems.\N这个名单可以一直列下去，包括惠普、戴尔和联想，每个人都知道如何构建这些系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:56.14,1:16:02.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the fact that we could squeeze Reuben Vera Reuben into this even though the\N所以我们能把 Vera Rubin 塞进这个系统，尽管
Dialogue: 0,1:16:03.02,1:16:09.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,performance is so much so much higher and very importantly the power is twice as high.\N性能高得多，而且更重要的是，功耗是原来的两倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:09.20,1:16:13.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,The power Vera Reuben is twice as high as Grace Hopper.\NVera Rubin 的功耗是 Grace Hopper 的两倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:13.71,1:16:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And yet and this is the miracle the air that goes into it, the the air flow is about the same.\N然而，这正是奇迹所在，进入其中的空气流量基本相同。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:21.96,1:16:27.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And very importantly the water that goes into it is the same temperature, 45°C.\N而且非常重要的是，进入其中的水温也相同，为45°C。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:27.40,1:16:33.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,With 45°C no water chillers are necessary for data centers.\N45°C的水温下，数据中心无需冷水机组。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:33.52,1:16:38.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're basically cooling this supercomputer with hot water.\N我们基本上是用热水来冷却这台超级计算机。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:38.32,1:16:41.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's so incredibly efficient.\N效率高得惊人。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:41.60,1:16:46.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is this is the new the new rack.\N所以这就是新的机架。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:46.09,1:16:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,1.7 times more transistors but five times more peak inference performance, three and a half times more peak um uh uh training performance.\N晶体管数量多出1.7倍，峰值推理性能提升五倍，峰值训练性能提升三倍半。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:57.40,1:17:02.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're connected on top using Spectrum-X.\N它们通过Spectrum-X连接在顶部。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:02.48,1:17:06.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank you.\N哦，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:06.92,1:17:16.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is this is the world's first manufacturing chip using uh TSMC's new process that we co-innovated called Co-op.\N这是世界上首款采用我们共同创新的台积电新工艺——Co-op制造的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:16.56,1:17:21.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a silicon photonics integrated silicon photonics process technology.\N这是一种硅光子集成工艺技术。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:21.40,1:17:26.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this allows us to take silicon photonics directly right to the chip.\N这使我们能够将硅光子技术直接做到芯片上。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:26.32,1:17:31.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is 512 ports at 200 gigabits per second.\N这是 512 个端口，每个端口速率为每秒 200 吉比特。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:31.56,1:17:36.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is the new Ethernet AI switch, the Spectrum-X Ethernet switch.\N这是新一代以太网 AI 交换机，Spectrum-X 以太网交换机。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:36.83,1:17:38.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And look at this giant chip.\N看看这个巨大的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:38.39,1:17:42.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But what's really amazing it's got silicon photonics directly connected to it.\N但真正惊人的是，它直接集成了硅光子技术。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:42.80,1:17:48.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And lasers come in.\N激光从这里输入。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:48.12,1:17:49.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Lasers come in through here.\N激光从这里进入。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:49.82,1:17:51.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Lasers come in through here.\N激光从这里进入。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:51.76,1:17:56.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,The optics are here and they connect out to the rest of the data data center.\N光学组件在这里，它们连接到数据中心的其余部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:57.04,1:18:06.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,This I'll show you in a second but this is on top of the rack and this is the new Spectrum-X silicon photonics switch.\N我稍后会向你们展示，但这是安装在机架顶部的，这是新的 Spectrum-X 硅光子交换机。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:06.56,1:18:07.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:18:07.48,1:18:10.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have something new I want to tell you about.\N我们还有个新东西要跟你们分享。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.14,1:18:19.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So just as I mentioned a couple years ago we introduced Spectrum-X so that we could reinvent the way that networking is done.\N就像我几年前提到的，我们推出了 Spectrum-X，以便重新定义网络技术的实现方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:19.28,1:18:26.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Ethernet is really easy to manage and everybody has an Ethernet stack and every data center in the world knows how to deal with Ethernet.\N以太网非常容易管理，每个人都有以太网协议栈，全球每个数据中心都懂得如何处理以太网。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:26.18,1:18:32.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the only thing that we were we were using at the time was called InfiniBand which is used for supercomputers.\N当时我们唯一使用的技术叫做 InfiniBand，它用于超级计算机。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:32.58,1:18:37.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,InfiniBand is very low latency um but of course the software stack,\NInfiniBand 的延迟非常低，但当然，它的软件栈，
Dialogue: 0,1:18:37.60,1:18:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,the entire manageability of InfiniBand is very alien to the people who use Ethernet.\N整个 InfiniBand 的管理方式对使用以太网的人来说非常陌生。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:42.20,1:18:46.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we decided to enter the Ethernet switch market for the very first time.\N于是我们决定首次进入以太网交换机市场。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:46.78,1:18:52.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Spectrum-X that just took off and it made us the largest networking company in the world as I mentioned.\NSpectrum-X 刚刚起飞，正如我所说，它让我们成为全球最大的网络公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.75,1:18:57.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,This this next generation Spectrum-X is going to carry on that tradition.\N这一代新一代的 Spectrum-X 将延续这一传统。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:57.16,1:19:01.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But just as I said earlier, AI has reinvented the whole computing stack.\N但正如我之前所说，AI 重新定义了整个计算架构。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:01.80,1:19:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every layer of the computing stack, it stands to reason that when AI starts to get deployed in the world's enterprises,\N计算架构的每一层，当 AI 开始在世界各大企业中部署时，
Dialogue: 0,1:19:08.64,1:19:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's going to also reinvent the way storage is done.\N它也必将重新定义存储方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:11.76,1:19:13.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, AI doesn't use SQL.\N但 AI 并不使用 SQL。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:13.56,1:19:16.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI use semantics information.\NAI 使用语义信息。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:16.64,1:19:24.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when AI is being used, it creates this temporary knowledge, temporary temporary memory called KV cache.\N当使用 AI 时，会产生一种临时知识，一种称为 KV 缓存的临时记忆。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:24.56,1:19:27.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Key value combination, but it's a KV cache.\N键值组合，但它就是 KV 缓存。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:27.06,1:19:30.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically, the cache of the AI, the working memory of the AI.\N基本上，这是 AI 的缓存，也就是 AI 的工作内存。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:30.96,1:19:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the working memory of the AI is stored in the HBM memory.\N而 AI 的工作内存存储在 HBM 内存中。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:35.12,1:19:43.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single token for every single token the GPU reads in the model, the entire model.\N对于每一个词元，GPU 都会读取整个模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:43.85,1:19:49.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It reads in the entire working memory and it produces one token.\N它读取整个工作内存，并生成一个词元。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:50.04,1:19:52.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it stores that one token back into the KV cache.\N然后将这个词元存储回 KV 缓存中。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:52.61,1:19:57.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the next the next time it does that, it reads in the entire memory,\N下一次执行时，它会读取整个内存，
Dialogue: 0,1:19:57.34,1:20:02.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,reads it and it streams it through our GPU and then generates another token.\N读取并将其通过我们的 GPU 流式传输，然后生成另一个词元。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:02.34,1:20:06.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, it does this repeatedly token after token after token and obviously,\N它就这样一个词元接一个词元地重复执行，显然，
Dialogue: 0,1:20:06.43,1:20:12.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you have a long conversation with that AI, over time that memory, that context memory is going to grow tremendously.\N如果你与 AI 进行长时间对话，随着时间推移，这种记忆、上下文记忆会急剧增长。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.58,1:20:17.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not to mention the models are growing, the number of turns that we're using the AIs are are are increasing.\N更不用说模型本身也在变大，我们使用 AI 的轮次也在不断增加。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:17.80,1:20:23.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We would like to have this AI stay with us our entire life and remember every single conversation we've ever had with it.\N我们希望这个AI能伴随我们一生，并记住我们与它之间的每一次对话。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:24.04,1:20:24.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:20:24.29,1:20:26.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single lick of research that I've asked it for.\N我所要求的每一项研究。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:26.78,1:20:31.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, with the number of people that will be sharing the supercomputer is going to continue to grow.\N当然，使用这台超级计算机的人数将持续增加。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:31.57,1:20:38.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this context memory which started out fitting inside an HBM is no longer large enough.\N因此，最初仅能装入HBM的上下文记忆，现在已不再够用。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:38.48,1:20:46.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Last year, we created Grace Blackwell's very fast memory we called fast context memory.\N去年，我们创建了Grace Blackwell的超快内存，我们称之为快速上下文内存。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:46.78,1:20:50.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,In That's the reason why we connected Grace directly to Hopper.\N这就是为什么我们将Grace直接连接到Hopper的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:50.84,1:20:56.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why we connected Grace directly to Blackwell so that we can expand the context memory.\N这就是为什么我们将Grace直接连接到Blackwell，以便扩展上下文记忆。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:56.45,1:20:58.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,But even that is not enough.\N但即便如此，仍然不够。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:58.05,1:21:06.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the next solution, of course, is to go off onto the network, the north-south network off to the storage of the company.\N因此，下一个解决方案显然是连接到网络，也就是南北向网络，连接到公司的存储系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:06.92,1:21:12.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you have a whole lot of AIs running at the same time, that network is no longer going to be fast enough.\N但如果同时运行大量AI，这个网络将不再足够快。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:13.04,1:21:16.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the answer is very clearly to do it different.\N所以，答案非常明确：必须换一种方式来做。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:16.65,1:21:28.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we we created BlueField 4 so that we could essentially have a very fast KV cache context memory store right in the rack.\N于是，我们推出了 BlueField 4，以便在机架内实现非常快速的键值缓存上下文内存存储。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:28.48,1:21:30.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I'll show you in just 1 second,\N接下来我用 1 秒时间向你展示，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:31.00,1:21:36.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,but there's a whole new category of storage systems and the industry is so excited because\N但这是一个全新的存储系统类别，整个行业都为此兴奋不已，因为
Dialogue: 0,1:21:36.73,1:21:41.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is a pain point for just about everybody who does a lot of token generation today,\N这是当今几乎所有进行大量词元生成的人所面临的痛点，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:41.77,1:21:44.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,the AI labs, the cloud service providers.\N包括 AI 实验室和云服务提供商。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:44.43,1:21:51.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're really suffering from the amount of network traffic that's causing being caused by KV cache moving around.\N他们正深受键值缓存频繁移动所导致的网络流量困扰。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:51.23,1:21:53.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the idea that we would create a new platform,\N于是，我们设想创建一个新平台，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:54.04,1:22:01.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,a new processor to run the entire Dynamo KV cache context memory management system\N一款新处理器，用于运行整个 Dynamo 键值缓存上下文内存管理系统，
Dialogue: 0,1:22:02.00,1:22:06.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,and to put it very close to the rest of the rack is completely revolutionary.\N并将其置于机架其余部分的附近，这完全是一次革命性突破。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:06.83,1:22:08.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is it.\N就是这样。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:08.28,1:22:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is it sits right here.\N它就在这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:11.44,1:22:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this this is all the compute nodes.\N这里全是计算节点。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:15.04,1:22:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of these is NVLink 72.\N每一个都是 NVLink 72。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:18.04,1:22:21.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is Vera Rubin NVLink 72.\N这就是 Vera Rubin NVLink 72。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:21.48,1:22:24.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,144 Rubin GPUs.\N144 个 Rubin GPU。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:24.68,1:22:27.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the context memory that's stored here.\N这是这里存储的上下文内存。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:27.13,1:22:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Behind each one of these are four BlueFields.\N每一个后面都有四个 BlueField。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:30.20,1:22:35.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Behind each BlueField is 150 terabytes of memory context memory.\N每个 BlueField 后面有 150 太字节的内存上下文。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:35.68,1:22:43.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for each GPU, once you allocate it across, each GPU will get an additional 16 terabytes.\N每个 GPU 分配后，每个 GPU 将额外获得 16 太字节。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:43.36,1:22:50.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, inside this node, each GPU essentially has 1 terabyte.\N现在，在这个节点内部，每个 GPU 实际上都有 1 太字节。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:50.08,1:22:58.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now, with this backing store here directly on the same east-west traffic at exactly the same data rate,\N现在，有了这个直接位于同一东西向流量上的后备存储，数据速率完全相同，
Dialogue: 0,1:22:58.12,1:23:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,200 gigabits per second across literally the entire fabric of this compute node, you're going to get an additional 16 terabytes of memory.\N每秒 200 吉比特，贯穿这个计算节点的整个结构，你将额外获得 16 太字节的内存。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:08.32,1:23:08.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:23:08.78,1:23:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is the management plane.\N这是管理平面。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:11.36,1:23:22.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are these are the Spectrum-X switches that connects all of them together.\N这些是连接所有设备的 Spectrum-X 交换机。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:22.40,1:23:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over here these switches at the end connects them to the rest of the data center.\N这些位于末端的交换机将它们连接到数据中心的其余部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:29.68,1:23:30.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:23:30.16,1:23:32.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this is the Vera Rubin.\N这就是 Vera Rubin。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:32.72,1:23:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, there's several things that's really incredible about it.\N它有几项非常令人惊叹的特性。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:35.84,1:23:44.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the first thing that I mentioned is that the this entire system is twice the energy efficiency,\N我提到的第一点是，整个系统能效提高了两倍，
Dialogue: 0,1:23:44.59,1:23:51.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially the the the temperature performance in the sense that that even though the power is twice as high,\N本质上，尽管功耗翻倍，
Dialogue: 0,1:23:51.55,1:24:01.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,the amount of energy used is twice as high, the amount of computation is many times higher than that, but the liquid that goes into it still 45°C.\N但能耗也翻倍，计算量却高出数倍，而进入系统的液冷温度仍保持在 45°C。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:01.40,1:24:05.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,That enables us to save about 6% of the world's data center power.\N这使我们能够节省全球数据中心约 6% 的电力。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:05.80,1:24:08.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that's a very big deal.\N这是一个非常了不起的成果。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.04,1:24:14.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second very big deal is that this entire system is now confidential computing safe.\N第二个重大突破是，整个系统现在具备机密计算安全性。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:14.71,1:24:19.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Meaning, everything is encoded in transit, at rest and during compute.\N意味着所有数据在传输中、静止时以及计算过程中均处于加密状态。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:19.60,1:24:23.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every single bus is now encrypted.\N而且每一辆公交车现在都已加密。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:23.44,1:24:34.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every PCI Express, every NVLink, every you know, NVLink between CPU and GPU, between GPU to GPU, everything is now encrypted.\N每一个 PCI Express 接口，每一个 NVLink，无论是 CPU 与 GPU 之间，\N还是 GPU 与 GPU 之间，所有连接现在都已加密。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:34.40,1:24:37.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it's confidential computing safe.\N因此，这是安全的机密计算。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:37.40,1:24:46.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,This allows companies to feel safe that their models are being deployed by somebody else, but it will never be seen by anybody else.\N这使得企业可以放心，他们的模型由他人部署，但绝不会被任何人看到。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:46.48,1:24:46.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:46.91,1:24:55.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this particular system is not only incredibly energy efficient, but there's one other thing that's incredible.\N因此，这个系统不仅能效极高，还有另一点令人惊叹。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:55.28,1:25:04.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because of the nature of the workload of AI, it spikes instantaneously with this computation layer called all reduce.\N由于 AI 工作负载的特性，这种称为 all reduce 的计算层会瞬间产生峰值。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:04.40,1:25:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The amount of current, the amount of energy that is used simultaneously is really off the charts.\N同时消耗的电流和能量量级实在惊人。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:09.88,1:25:12.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Often times, they'll spike up 25%.\N通常会瞬间上升 25%。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:12.92,1:25:23.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,We now have power smoothing across the entire system so that you don't have to over provision by 25 times or if you over provision by 25 times,\N现在我们实现了整个系统的电力平滑，因此无需再超额配置 25 倍，或者即使超额配置 25 倍，
Dialogue: 0,1:25:23.14,1:25:29.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,you don't have to leave 25% of the energy um squandered or unused.\N也不必浪费或闲置 25% 的能源。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:29.27,1:25:35.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so now, you could fill up the entire power budget and you don't have to provision beyond that.\N现在你可以充分利用全部电力预算，而无需再额外预留。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:35.80,1:25:38.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the last thing, of course, is performance.\N然后最后一点，当然是性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:38.48,1:25:40.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, let's take a look at the performance of this.\N那么，让我们来看看它的性能表现。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:40.29,1:25:44.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are only charts that people who build AI supercomputers would love.\N这些图表只有构建 AI 超级计算机的人才会喜欢。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:44.35,1:25:46.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,It took every single one of these chips,\N我们用到了每一颗芯片，
Dialogue: 0,1:25:46.67,1:25:52.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,complete redesign of every single one of the systems and rewriting the entire stack for us to make this possible.\N对每个系统进行了彻底重新设计，并为我们重写了整个软件栈，才让这一切成为可能。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:52.88,1:25:57.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically, this is training the AI model, this first column.\N基本上，这是在训练 AI 模型，第一列就是这个。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:57.28,1:26:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,The faster you train AI models the faster you can get the next frontier out to the world.\N你训练 AI 模型的速度越快，就越能快速将下一个前沿技术推向世界。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:02.32,1:26:03.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is your time to market.\N这就是你的上市时间。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:03.65,1:26:05.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is technology leadership.\N这就是技术领导力。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.40,1:26:07.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is your pricing power.\N这就是你的定价能力。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:07.84,1:26:14.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, in the case of the green, this is essentially a 10 trillion parameter model.\N因此，绿色这一栏本质上是一个 10 万亿参数的模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:14.53,1:26:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We scaled it up from Deep Seek.\N我们是从 Deep Seek 扩展而来的。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:16.40,1:26:18.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Deep Seek That's why we call it Deep Seek plus plus.\N深Seek 这就是我们称之为 Deep Seek 加加的原因。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:18.78,1:26:24.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,A training a 10 trillion parameter model on 100 trillion tokens.\N在 10 万亿词元上训练一个 10 万亿参数的模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:24.76,1:26:25.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:26:25.19,1:26:31.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's this is our simulation projection of what it would take for us to build the next frontier model.\N这是我们模拟预测的，要构建下一个前沿模型所需的成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:31.21,1:26:37.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next frontier model uh Elon's already mentioned that the next version of Grok, Grok 5, I think is 7 trillion parameters.\N下一个前沿模型，埃隆已经提到过，Grok 的下一个版本 Grok 5，我认为是 7 万亿参数。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:37.60,1:26:38.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is 10.\N所以，这是 10 万亿。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:38.56,1:26:41.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and the green is Blackwell.\N绿色部分代表 Blackwell。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:41.64,1:26:50.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here, in the case of um uh Rubin, notice the throughput is so much higher and therefore,\N在 Rubin 的情况下，注意吞吐量高得多，因此，
Dialogue: 0,1:26:50.35,1:26:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,it only takes 1/4 as many of these systems in order to train the model in the time that we gave it here, which is 1 month.\N只需要四分之一数量的系统，就能在我们设定的 1 个月内完成模型训练。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:59.68,1:27:00.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:27:00.62,1:27:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so time time is the same for everybody.\N所以，时间对每个人来说都是一样的。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:03.84,1:27:09.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, how much how fast you can train that model and how large a model you can train is how you're going to get to the frontier first.\N现在，你训练模型的速度有多快，以及你能训练多大的模型，将决定你能否率先达到前沿。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:09.99,1:27:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second part is your factory throughput.\N第二部分是你的工厂吞吐量。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:13.60,1:27:22.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Blackwell is green again and factory throughput is important because your factory is in the case of a gigawatt is $50 billion.\N黑尔威尔再次变得高效，而工厂吞吐量至关重要，因为一个吉瓦级别的工厂价值500亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:22.57,1:27:29.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,A $50 billion data center can only consume 1 gigawatt of power.\N一个500亿美元的数据中心仅能消耗1吉瓦的电力。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:29.56,1:27:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, if your performance your throughput per watt is very good versus quite poor, that directly translates to your revenues.\N因此，如果你每瓦特的性能和吞吐量表现优异，远超表现平庸的情况，这将直接转化为你的收入。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:41.12,1:27:46.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Your revenues of your data center is directly related to the second second column.\N你的数据中心收入与第二列数据直接相关。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.93,1:27:51.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in the case of Blackwell, it was about 10 times over Hopper.\N在黑尔威尔的情况下，这比霍珀高出约10倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:51.41,1:27:55.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the case of Rubin, it's going to be about 10 times higher again.\N在Rubin的情况下，这一数字还将再提高约10倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:55.48,1:27:56.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:27:56.15,1:28:06.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in the case of now, the um the cost of the tokens, how cost-effectively it is to generate the token this is Rubin about 1/10.\N而现在，词元的成本，即生成词元的效率，Rubin约为之前的十分之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:07.03,1:28:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just as in the case of Yep.\N就像在耶普的情况一样。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.68,1:28:24.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that's how This is how we're going to get everybody to the next frontier to um push AI to the next level.\N这就是我们将所有人推向下一个前沿、推动AI达到新高度的方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:24.20,1:28:30.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course, to build these data centers energy efficiently and cost efficiently.\N当然，还要以高效且低成本的方式建设这些数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:30.48,1:28:31.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is it.\N所以，这就是最终成果。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:31.80,1:28:33.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is NVIDIA today.\N这就是今天的英伟达。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:33.08,1:28:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we mentioned that we build chips, but as you know, NVIDIA builds entire systems now.\N你们知道，我们提到过我们制造芯片，但正如你们所知，英伟达如今已经构建完整的系统。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:40.60,1:28:43.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And AI is a full stack.\N而 AI 是一个全栈技术。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:43.64,1:28:50.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we're reinventing AI across everything from chips to infrastructure to models to applications.\N我们正在从芯片到基础设施，再到模型和应用，全面重塑 AI。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:50.83,1:28:58.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And our job is to create the entire stack so that all of you could create incredible applications uh for the rest of the world.\N我们的目标是打造完整的技术栈，让你们所有人都能为世界创造令人惊叹的应用。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:58.22,1:28:59.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you all for coming.\N感谢大家的到来。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:59.50,1:29:01.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have a great CES.\N祝大家 CES 顺利。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:01.96,1:29:10.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now Before Before I Before I let you guys go, uh there were a whole bunch of slides we have to we have to leave on the cutting floor.\N在你们离开之前，还有一大堆幻灯片我们不得不留在剪辑台上。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:10.47,1:29:11.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we have some outtakes here.\N所以，这里有一些花絮。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:11.98,1:29:14.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it'll be fun for you.\N我觉得你们会喜欢的。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:14.17,1:29:20.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have a great CES, guys.\N祝大家 CES 玩得开心，伙计们。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:20.36,1:29:24.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And cut.\N拍摄开始。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:24.80,1:29:27.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,NVIDIA live at CES take four.\N英伟达在 CES 现场直播第四次。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:27.90,1:29:28.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Marker.\N位置标记。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:28.72,1:29:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Boom mic.\N话筒准备。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:30.72,1:29:33.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Action.\N开始。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:33.84,1:29:36.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sorry guys.\N对不起各位。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:36.53,1:29:41.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Platform shift, huh?\N平台转变，是吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:29:41.24,1:29:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,That should do it.\N这样应该就可以了。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:42.60,1:29:46.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And let's roll camera.\N现在开始摄像机。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:46.68,1:29:49.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,A shade of green.\N一种绿色。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:49.20,1:29:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,A bright happy green.\N一种明亮欢快的绿色。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:51.52,1:30:01.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,World's most powerful AI supercomputer you can plug into the wall next to my toaster.\N世界上你唯一能插在烤面包机旁边的墙上的最强大的 AI 超级计算机。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:01.40,1:30:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey guys, I'm I'm stuck again.\N嘿，伙计们，我又卡住了。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:02.84,1:30:03.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry.\N对不起啊。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:03.76,1:30:04.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,This slide is never going to work.\N这页幻灯片根本行不通。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:04.89,1:30:06.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's just cut it.\N我们干脆删掉吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:06.56,1:30:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello?\N喂？
Dialogue: 0,1:30:07.36,1:30:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me?\N你能听到我吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:30:11.28,1:30:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like I was saying, the router because not every problem needs the biggest, smartest model.\N就像我刚才说的，路由器不需要每个问题都用最大、最聪明的模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:17.52,1:30:19.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just the right one.\N只需要合适的那个就行。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:19.92,1:30:23.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. No. Don't lose any of them.\N不要，不要丢掉任何一个。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:23.20,1:30:30.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,This new six-chip Rubin platform makes one amazing AI supercomputer.\N这个全新的六芯片Rubin平台，能打造一台惊人的AI超级计算机。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:30.36,1:30:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,There you go, little guy.\N给你，小家伙。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:32.16,1:30:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, no. No, not the scaling laws.\N哦不，不要，别碰缩放定律。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:35.36,1:30:36.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,There is a squirrel on the car.\N有一只松鼠在车上。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:36.98,1:30:39.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Be ready to make the squirrel go away.\N准备好让松鼠离开。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:39.14,1:30:41.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ask the squirrel gently to move away.\N轻声请松鼠走开。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:41.84,1:30:48.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did you know the best models today are all mixture of experts?\N你知道吗，目前最好的模型都是专家混合模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:48.60,1:31:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey.\N嘿。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:00.16,1:31:03.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where'd everybody go?\N大家都去哪儿了？
